(D16: &arena_value = the .rodata ANS- literal; bypass len 65536)\n169\t   lib/*/libapp.so + libflutter.so  Flutter: strings libapp.so; flutter_assets/kernel_blob.bin (debug = source text)\n170\t   assets/index.android.bundle      RN: head -c8 | xxd; c61fbc03 = Hermes -> hbc-decompiler; else webcrack/js-beautify\n171\t   assemblies/*.dll|*.blob, libmonodroid.so   Xamarin: XALZ = lz4 per-dll; then ilspycmd f.dll\n172\t   libil2cpp.so + global-metadata.dat         Unity IL2CPP: strings global-metadata.dat | grep ANS- ; Managed/*.dll -> ilspycmd\n173\t   assets/www/, cordova.js, capacitor.config  hybrid JS: grep -r in assets/www\n174\t   assets/*.dex|*.jar|*.apk|*.zip|*.bin       dynamic code loading (D20: plain dex, ANS- const in `...payload.Module`):\n175\t                                    strings -a it first; no dex/PK/ELF magic -> xor/known-plaintext unwrap (key from host dex);\n176\t                                    >1 payload -> the one matching the host's pinned digest; >1 ANS- -> the member the host\n177\t                                    names (`<entry>:<class>` string, `moduleContract`), never the first regex hit\n178\t   libjiagu/libsecexe/libDexHelper.so          packer: payload is the encrypted asset; static decrypt or give up early\n179\t   res/xml/network_security_config.xml        NSC: aapt dump xmltree x.apk res/xml/network_security_config.xml\n180\t   resources.arsc                   aapt dump --values resources x.apk | grep -iE 'ans-|secret|key|flag|token'\n181\t   *.db / shared_prefs/*.xml / *.ab sqlite3 f.db .dump ; .ab: dd bs=24 skip=1 | zlib-flate -uncompress | tar x\n182\t   res/raw/*.bks|*.p12|*.pem        keystore: password is a dex string; keytool -list -v -storepass PW\n183\t   google-services.json / firebase  key/URL itself may be the answer\n184\t   base.apk + split_config.*.apk / manifest.json / toc.pb / BundleConfig.pb   split/XAPK/APKS/AAB: unzip inner, recurse\n185\t   Payload/*.app/                   iOS: plistlib Info.plist; rz-bin -zz the Mach-O\n186\t2. Plain-anywhere scan (incl. UTF-16 the zip scan misses):\n187\t   for f in $(unzip -Z1 x.apk); do unzip -p x.apk \"$f\" | strings -a -el | grep -H --label=\"$f\" ANS-; done\n188\t   7z l x.apk vs unzip -l x.apk differ -> zip tricks (dup entry / trailing data): binwalk x.apk\n189\t3. Manifest (fast): aapt dump xmltree x.apk AndroidManifest.xml | grep -E \\\n190\t   'exported|scheme|host|autoVerify|permission|debuggable|allowBackup|usesCleartext|networkSecurity|taskAffinity|launchMode|meta-data'\n191\t   meta-data value= is a hiding spot (huntress.mechanic lives there). debuggable=true (D21) is a fact, not an answer.\n192\t4. Dex triage: strings -a classes*.dex | grep -E 'DAY-|CODEC|ANS-|^[0-9A-F]{8,16}$' then map API hits to themes:\n193\t   DexClassLoader/InMemoryDexClassLoader/moduleContract -> asset dex   SecretKeySpec/AES/Cipher -> static key decrypt\n194\t   loadLibrary/RegisterNatives -> .so                     java/util/Random/setSeed/currentTimeMillis -> regenerate RNG\n195\t   MessageDigest/PBKDF2 -> hash brute                     addJavascriptInterface/loadUrl/file:///android_asset -> assets html/js\n196\t   Binder/$Stub/Messenger/onReceive -> IPC handler        CertificatePinner/sha256/ -> pins in code or NSC\n197\t   su/magisk/goldfish/frida/TracerPid/isDebuggerConnected/debuggerGate (D21)/rootSignals (D22) -> clean_device_scan:\n198\t   clean-path value PER SIGNAL; never force the aggregate isRooted()/success flag (D22 \"without globally patching\")\n199\t   Class.forName/getDeclaredMethod -> reflection_scan     BuildConfig / R$string -> arsc / BuildConfig.java\n200\t   Proxy/MethodHandles/invoke-custom -> real target; packed-switch in a loop / $SwitchMap$ -> flattened_cfg_scan\n201\t   KeyStore.getInstance(\"BKS\"|\"PKCS12\") -> res/raw keystore + password string\n202\t5. Read code only after 1-4: droidasc findrefs x.apk string <hit>; droidasc getclass x.apk <cls>; jadx -d w/jadx x.apk\n203\t   (add --deobf for 1-2 letter class names). Strings split across constants: rebuild order from the method body.\n204\t   String decryptors (D18 TT `EncryptedStrings.decryptByte`): dex_eval_scan, else jadx the helper, take the ARGS from\n205\t   each call site, re-implement in py; unknown key/rolling scheme -> solve it from the ANS- known plaintext.\n206\t   R8/decoys (D17): hint strings like \"follow b -> a and ignore field c\" name the chain; >1 ANS- candidate -> keep\n207\t   the one appended before `proof=` in ChallengeActivity, never the first regex hit. Reflection/dispatch (D19 theme):\n208\t   names may be encoded or picked by a key from the deep link/asset; evaluate only the invoked target, not its twins.\n209\t   lib scanners for code-side answers (not in extract_answer): renamed_chain_scan, proof_flow_scan, dex_eval_scan,\n210\t   reflection_scan, mapping_restore_scan, signing_block_scan, zip_structure_scan  (all lib.android, take apk path)\n211\t6. Native, if no literal: rizin -A -qc 'iE; izz~ANS; afl' f.so ; pdf @ sym.Java_... ; xor loops -> py capstone/unicorn.\n212\t7. Validate: candidate must fullmatch ^ANS-[0-9A-F]{16}$ (uppercase). Two sources (asset + .so) agreeing = submit.\n213\t8. Mastery: each set can be a different day's fixture; decode every APK on its own; loop over all answer_ids (3/5/6).\n214\t```\n215\t\n216\t## Readiness gaps\n217\t\n218\tPriority 1 = plausible within ~3 days. \"prebuild\" = pure-python extractor in `lib/android.py` style that races in\n219\t`solve.py`. \"tool\" = install. \"note\" = doc/prompt change. Already built (prebuild-state ok, dropped from the list):\n220\taab-proto-manifest-parse, ans-prefix-numeric-compose, anti-debug-state-machine-clean-path, apk-signing-block-payload,\n221\tasset-cipher-dex-loader, asset-db-prefs-backup, attestation-jws-claims, binder-ontransact-code-map,\n222\tbroadcast-receiver-action-map, cdex-vdex-string-pool, cert-and-signing-facts, cert-pin-and-nsc-facts,\n223\tclassloader-shadow-resolve, clean-device-env-stubs, custom-alphabet-decode, dalvik-mini-interpreter,\n224\tdart-snapshot-string-pool, decode-any-chain-peel, decrypt-call-site-args-eval, dex-bytecode-integrity-gate,\n225\tdex-gated-branch-consts, dex-native-call-args, dex-native-split-assembly, dex-slack-and-header-anomaly,\n226\tdex-string-decrypt-arrays, dispatch-key-resolve, emulator-telephony-sensor-stubs, entry-reachable-callgraph-rank,\n227\tenum-switchmap-state-resolve, exception-driven-control-flow, flattened-cfg-switch-eval, hermes-hbc-string-table,\n228\thook-framework-introspection-stubs, identifier-collision-resolve, identity-derived-key, il2cpp-metadata-literals,\n229\tintegrity-derived-key, java-serialized-object-parse, jni-export-return-trace, jni-gate-bypass-input,\n230\tjni-reflection-callback, jwt-token-decode-verify, known-string-obfuscator-signatures,\n231\tkotlin-metadata-names-and-coroutines, messagedigest-derived-answer, module-contract-member-eval, multi-abi-arm-native,\n232\tmulti-stage-loader-recurse, native-gated-branch-read, native-init-array-decrypt, native-libc-probe-stubs-emulate,\n233\tnative-payload-system-load, native-so-emulate-export, native-stack-string, nested-container-recurse,\n234\topaque-predicate-dead-branch, payload-digest-pinned-select, payload-magic-known-plaintext-unwrap,\n235\tpermutation-transposition-family, proguard-mapping-restore, proof-flow-candidate-ranking, protobuf-asset-wire-decode,\n236\tproxy-methodhandle-invokecustom, puzzle-entry-pointer-follow, puzzle-indexed-and-perm-fields, r8-renamed-chain-follow,\n237\treflection-name-resolve, registernatives-table, resource-id-const-resolve, rolling-xor-keystream-family,\n238\tsqlcipher-asset-decrypt, static-key-cipher-decode, timing-and-debug-flag-probe-stubs, tiny-bytecode-vm-interpret,\n239\tutf16-string-pool-scan, v1-manifest-digest-verify, webview-asset-js-scan, xamarin-xalz-blob-unpack,\n240\tzip-structure-anomaly-scan.\n241\tForecast after D22: the arc is walking MASVS-RESILIENCE one control per day (D21 anti-debug, D22 root). Next most likely:\n242\temulator detection, hook/Frida detection, tamper/installer/signature checks, attestation (key attestation `RootOfTrust`,\n243\tPlay Integrity), then obfuscation capstones. Code-side gates have never shipped (TT dex only names the mechanic:\n244\t`debuggerGate`, `rootSignals`); the gaps below harden the clean-device evaluator for the day one does.\n245\t\n246\t```json\n247\t[\n248\t  {\"id\": \"root-signal-vector-key\", \"concept\": \"multi-signal root detection where each probe contributes a bit/weight/fragment and the answer is derived from the whole clean vector (rows 47, 94)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D22 prompt: 'Model and bypass multiple synthetic root signals without globally patching success'; TT dex string `rootSignals`. Expected real version: N probe methods (su paths, Build.TAGS test-keys, magisk/superuser packages, ro.debuggable/ro.secure, rw /system mount, which su, SELinux) each returning boolean/int; results combined by or-int/shl-int into a mask, summed into a score vs threshold, or appended as fragments; the mask/score keys an xor/hash that yields the ANS- value, so forcing isRooted()/success=true at the aggregate gives a DECOY. Build `root_signal_scan(apk)`: locate probe methods (methods whose bodies hit the clean_device_scan probe table), evaluate each with clean retail-phone answers through the Dalvik evaluator, then evaluate the combiner method with those per-signal results (not with a forced aggregate). Report the clean-vector value first; also report (labelled, demoted) the value from a forced-success path so the solver can tell them apart. Handle signals stored in a boolean[]/int[]/BitSet/EnumSet/Map<String,Boolean>. Budget <0.8 s, never raise.\"},\n249\t  {\"id\": \"probe-arg-resolve-before-stub\", \"concept\": \"root/emulator probe arguments built at runtime (split, reversed, xor'd paths and package names) so the stub must see the computed string (rows 47, 48, 94)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"clean_device_scan keys its answers on literal strings (`/system/xbin/su`, `com.topjohnwu.magisk`, `test-keys`). A real root gate hides them: `new File(dec(\\\"...\\\")).exists()`, `\\\"/sys\\\"+\\\"tem/\\\"+\\\"bin/su\\\"`, reversed `us/nib/metsys/`, char arrays, base64. Make every probe stub match on the EVALUATED argument (after the evaluator runs the decoder/StringBuilder) and normalise it (collapse //, strip trailing /, casefold) before lookup; unknown paths under /system,/sbin,/su,/data/local,/data/adb,/cache -> non-existent; unknown package names containing magisk/supersu/kingroot/xposed/lsposed/zygisk/frida -> NameNotFoundException. Log each (probe, resolved arg, stub answer) so the worker can audit. Synthetic test: path assembled from 3 fragments and a 1-byte xor.\"},\n250\t  {\"id\": \"process-exec-shell-probe-stubs\", \"concept\": \"Runtime.exec / ProcessBuilder shell probes with stubbed process I/O (row 95)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Root checks often run `which su`, `su -c id`, `getprop ro.build.tags`, `getprop ro.debuggable`, `mount`, `getenforce`, `id`, `ls /data/adb`. Stub in the Dalvik evaluator: Runtime.getRuntime().exec(String|String[]) and new ProcessBuilder(..).start() -> a fake Process whose getInputStream yields clean output per command (which su -> '' ; su -> IOException 'Cannot run program'; getprop ro.build.tags -> 'release-keys'; ro.debuggable -> '0'; ro.secure -> '1'; getenforce -> 'Enforcing'; id -> 'uid=10123(u0_a123) gid=10123'; mount / cat /proc/mounts -> '/dev/block/dm-0 /system ext4 ro,seclabel,relatime 0 0' lines, no magisk/tmpfs on /system), waitFor/exitValue -> 1 for which/su, 0 otherwise; InputStreamReader/BufferedReader.readLine/Scanner/readText over it; File('/proc/mounts'|'/proc/self/mountinfo') reads -> same clean text. Command arg resolved via probe-arg-resolve-before-stub.\"},\n251\t  {\"id\": \"key-attestation-rootoftrust-parse\", \"concept\": \"Android hardware key attestation: parse the KeyDescription / RootOfTrust extension from shipped certs (row 93)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D22's title 'Root of Trust' is the ASN.1 RootOfTrust in key attestation (OID 1.3.6.1.4.1.11129.2.1.17 KeyDescription -> teeEnforced/softwareEnforced AuthorizationList tag [704] rootOfTrust = SEQUENCE{verifiedBootKey OCTET STRING, deviceLocked BOOLEAN, verifiedBootState ENUM(0 Verified,1 SelfSigned,2 Unverified,3 Failed), verifiedBootHash OCTET STRING}; also attestationChallenge, attestationSecurityLevel, attestationApplicationId [709] with package name + signature digests, osVersion [705], osPatchLevel [706]). Build `key_attestation_scan(apk)`: find DER/PEM certs and chains in any entry (assets/res/raw/META-INF/puzzle JSON base64 fields; `-----BEGIN CERTIFICATE`, 30 82 DER), parse with a minimal pure-python DER walker (no subprocess), extract the extension, decode the AuthorizationList, report all fields; ANS- regex on challenge/octet strings (also hex/ASCII of verifiedBootHash); compare attestationApplicationId signature digest to signing_certs(apk) and verifiedBootState to the dex constants the app compares. Clean = Verified + deviceLocked true.\"},\n252\t  {\"id\": \"installer-source-and-tamper-probe-stubs\", \"concept\": \"anti-tamper / repackaging probes: installer source, signature, debuggable flag, dex CRC (rows 49, 50)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"After root/emulator/hook the arc names tamper checks. Extend the clean-device probe table: PackageManager.getInstallerPackageName / getInstallSourceInfo().getInstallingPackageName / getInitiatingPackageName -> 'com.android.vending'; getPackageInfo(own, GET_SIGNATURES|GET_SIGNING_CERTIFICATES).signatures/signingInfo.getApkContentsSigners -> the APK's REAL v1/v2 cert bytes from signing_certs(apk) (so hashCode/MessageDigest comparisons evaluate on the true digest); ApplicationInfo.flags FLAG_DEBUGGABLE bit from the manifest; ApplicationInfo.sourceDir/publicSourceDir -> '/data/app/<pkg>-1/base.apk'; ZipFile(sourceDir).getEntry('classes.dex').getCrc() -> the real CRC from the APK; Context.getPackageCodePath likewise. Integrate with dex_integrity_gate_scan / integrity_key_scan (built) so a digest-keyed answer uses real bytes. Report the value on the untampered path.\"},\n253\t  {\"id\": \"worker-cue-inline\", \"concept\": \"unseen-theme routing\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Inline the 'Recognition cues' block above into the mobile worker prompt (skills/huntress-ctf mobile skill) so an unseen container (Flutter/RN/Xamarin/asset dex) is routed in 1-2 turns; add step 2's UTF-16 scan to triage.md pre-extraction.\"},\n254\t  {\"id\": \"native-system-property-and-mounts-stubs\", \"concept\": \"native root/emulator probes via __system_property_get, popen and /proc/self/mounts inside the .so (rows 66, 95)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"native-libc-probe-stubs-emulate (built) covers ptrace/TracerPid/access/stat. Add unicorn import stubs: __system_property_get(name, buf) / __system_property_find + __system_property_read(_callback) -> clean values (ro.build.tags release-keys, ro.debuggable 0, ro.secure 1, ro.boot.verifiedbootstate green, ro.boot.flash.locked 1, ro.kernel.qemu '', ro.hardware a real SoC); popen/pclose + fgets for 'which su'/'getprop'/'mount' -> clean text; fopen('/proc/self/mounts'|'/proc/mounts'|'/proc/self/mountinfo') -> lines without magisk/tmpfs-on-/system/overlay; opendir/readdir on /data/adb, /sbin -> empty; dlopen of libmagisk/libfrida -> NULL. Same import resolution path (pyelftools .rela.plt), x86_64 then arm64.\"},\n255\t  {\"id\": \"native-inline-syscall-stubs\", \"concept\": \"native probes issuing raw syscalls (svc #0 / syscall instruction) to bypass libc hooks\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Hardened root/anti-hook checks call openat/faccessat/readlinkat/newfstatat/ptrace/getppid directly via `syscall` (x86_64) or `svc #0` (arm64) so Frida libc hooks miss them. In the unicorn runner, hook UC_HOOK_INSN syscall (x86_64) / UC_HOOK_INTR (arm64), dispatch on rax/x8 number (x86_64: openat 257, faccessat 269, newfstatat 262, readlinkat 267, read 0, close 3, ptrace 101, getppid 110; arm64: openat 56, faccessat 48, newfstatat 79, readlinkat 78, read 63, close 57, ptrace 117, getppid 173) and answer from the same clean filesystem/proc model as the libc stubs (ENOENT for su paths, fake fd for /proc/self/status with TracerPid 0). Test with a tiny hand-assembled .so.\"},\n256\t  {\"id\": \"play-integrity-verdict-select\", \"concept\": \"Play Integrity / SafetyNet verdict JSON drives the branch: pick the value for the strongest clean verdict (row 87)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"attestation-jws-claims (built) decodes tokens. Add verdict semantics: parse decoded payloads or plain JSON assets with requestDetails{requestPackageName, nonce, timestampMillis}, appIntegrity{appRecognitionVerdict PLAY_RECOGNIZED|UNRECOGNIZED_VERSION|UNEVALUATED, packageName, certificateSha256Digest[], versionCode}, deviceIntegrity{deviceRecognitionVerdict [MEETS_BASIC_INTEGRITY, MEETS_DEVICE_INTEGRITY, MEETS_STRONG_INTEGRITY, MEETS_VIRTUAL_INTEGRITY]}, accountDetails{appLicensingVerdict LICENSED}, legacy SafetyNet ctsProfileMatch/basicIntegrity/evaluationType HARDWARE_BACKED. When several verdict blobs or dex branches exist, rank the one with PLAY_RECOGNIZED + MEETS_DEVICE/STRONG_INTEGRITY + LICENSED + certificateSha256Digest equal to signing_certs(apk) + nonce matching the host's computed nonce; report the ANS- value tied to it; demote others as decoys.\"},\n257\t  {\"id\": \"biometric-auth-callback-eval\", \"concept\": \"MASVS-AUTH biometric / local auth bypass: the success callback holds the secret (row 92)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Untouched MASVS group. Find classes extending androidx.biometric.BiometricPrompt$AuthenticationCallback, android.hardware.biometrics.BiometricPrompt$AuthenticationCallback or FingerprintManager(Compat)$AuthenticationCallback, KeyguardManager.createConfirmDeviceCredentialIntent + onActivityResult(RESULT_OK). Evaluate onAuthenticationSucceeded(result) with a result whose getCryptoObject() returns null (event-bound bypass) AND with a CryptoObject wrapping a stub Cipher (doFinal = identity) -- report both values labelled; evaluate onActivityResult with resultCode -1. Also flag `setUserAuthenticationRequired(false)` / missing `setInvalidatedByBiometricEnrollment`. ANS- regex on the results; demote values reached only on onAuthenticationFailed/onAuthenticationError.\"},\n258\t  {\"id\": \"pyxamstore\", \"concept\": \"Xamarin assemblies.blob / XALZ (row 55)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"pip: `uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python pyxamstore` (or github jakev/pyxamstore). Then `pyxamstore unpack -d assemblies/` and ilspycmd. Also small prebuild: XALZ header (magic, index, size) + lz4.block decompress (lz4 in venv).\"},\n259\t  {\"id\": \"apkid\", \"concept\": \"packer / obfuscator / anti-VM identification (rows 44-48)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"pip: `uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python apkid` (needs yara-python, already OK). `apkid -j x.apk` names packers, obfuscators and anti-debug in one call: a fast routing cue for an unseen theme.\"},\n260\t  {\"id\": \"bundletool\", \"concept\": \"AAB / APKS packaging (row 58)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github release jar google/bundletool (bundletool-all-1.17.x.jar) into tools/bundletool + bin shim. `bundletool dump manifest --bundle x.aab`, `bundletool build-apks --mode=universal`. AAB manifests are protobuf, so aapt dump xmltree fails on them.\"},\n261\t  {\"id\": \"whitebox-table-cipher-eval\", \"concept\": \"white-box / table-driven cipher (lookup-table AES or byte S-box chains) as an obfuscation capstone\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"After VM/flattening the next obfuscation step is table-based crypto with the key folded into large static arrays (int[256]/byte[4096] T-boxes, Tyi tables, or chained byte S-boxes) in dex <clinit> or .so .rodata. Don't recover the key: evaluate the table walk. Dex: dex_array_scan to pull the arrays, then run the decrypt method in the Dalvik evaluator with arrays preloaded (raise its step budget for 10-16 rounds of aget/xor); .so: unicorn-run the export over .rodata tables. Fallback: if the method is a pure byte-wise S-box chain, compose the tables in python and invert via the ANS- known plaintext. Budget <0.8 s.\"},\n262\t  {\"id\": \"ios-ipa-readiness\", \"concept\": \"iOS IPA (row 64)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Lane is named mobile-android; if an .ipa ever ships: unzip Payload/, plistlib for Info.plist and binary plists, rz-bin -zz / lief for Mach-O strings, ipsw (github blacktop/ipsw release) for class-dump. Nothing to prebuild now.\"},\n263\t  {\"id\": \"il2cppdumper\", \"concept\": \"Unity IL2CPP (row 56)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github release Perfare/Il2CppDumper (or SamboyCoding/Cpp2IL) into tools/; run with bin/dotnet. Only if a Unity fixture ever ships.\"},\n264\t  {\"id\": \"blutter\", \"concept\": \"Flutter Dart AOT (row 52)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github worawit/blutter (python3 blutter.py <lib dir> <out>; builds per Dart version with cmake/ninja + fetches the Dart SDK, slow first run; arm64 only). Alt: pip reflutter (needs repack + device: low value). Plain strings on libapp.so cover literal answers.\"},\n265\t  {\"id\": \"abe\", \"concept\": \"encrypted Android backup (row 16)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github release nelenkov/android-backup-extractor (abe.jar): `java -jar abe.jar unpack b.ab b.tar [pw]`. Needed only for encrypted .ab (PBKDF2+AES); unencrypted is zlib-flate.\"},\n266\t  {\"id\": \"frida-tools\", \"concept\": \"dynamic instrumentation / root and frida checks (rows 47, 48)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"pip frida-tools / objection. Low value: no Android device or emulator here (adb present, no target), and every answer so far was static. Keep the rule: read the gated branch statically.\"},\n267\t  {\"id\": \"standalone-baksmali\", \"concept\": \"smali-level reading / patching (row 51)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"Link tools/dex2jar/d2j-baksmali.sh + d2j-smali.sh into bin/ (already on disk), or github google/smali release. apktool d already emits smali, so cosmetic.\"}\n268\t]\n269\t```"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c40b34bd-42fb-42e5-b584-d0c2bd140aef","uuid":"dad29528-fed8-4ef1-aed8-ff3e93895399","timestamp":"2026-10-23T13:31:23.696Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/coverage/mobile-android.md","content":"| 20 | Logcat leakage | gap | `Log.d(tag, secret)` constant in dex | `Landroid/util/Log;`, tag strings near secret | `strings -a classes*.dex`; `jadx` grep `Log\\.` | med |\n| 21 | Clipboard / screenshot / keyboard cache | gap | n/a (fact question) | `ClipboardManager`, `FLAG_SECURE`, `textNoSuggestions` | `jadx`, `apktool d` | low-med |\n| 22 | Hardcoded secret in strings.xml / BuildConfig | gap | `resources.arsc` string, `BuildConfig` static field | `resources.arsc` present, `BuildConfig` class, `api_key`/`secret` res names | `aapt dump --values resources x.apk \\| grep -B2 ANS-` [i]; `apktool d` + `grep -r ANS- out/res`; `jadx` `BuildConfig.java` | high: cheapest escalation |\n| 23 | Firebase / google-services misconfig | gap | `firebase_database_url`, `google_api_key` res or `google-services.json` | `firebaseio.com`, `AIza[0-9A-Za-z_-]{35}`, `google_app_id` | `apktool d` + grep; offline (answer = the key/URL or a JSON in assets) | med |\n| 24 | Cloud/API keys (AWS, Stripe, JWT, OAuth) | gap | dex/arsc cons