point stall detection) | gap | value on the fast (un-stepped) path | two `SystemClock.elapsedRealtime`/`uptimeMillis`/`System.nanoTime`/`Debug.threadCpuTimeNanos` reads + `sub-long` + `cmp-long` vs a const | `jadx`; evaluate with small monotonic deltas (`timing-and-debug-flag-probe-stubs`) | high: natural real version of D21 |\n| 89 | Enum / sealed-class state machine (`$SwitchMap$`, Kotlin `$WhenMappings`) | gap | the case reached from the initial state through clean transitions | synthetic `<Outer>$1`/`$WhenMappings` with `int[]` filled in `<clinit>` (`aput` under NoSuchFieldError catch), `ordinal()`, `values()` | `jadx` prints the `switch`; `enum-switchmap-state-resolve` prebuild | high: \"state machine\" wording |\n| 90 | Exception-driven control flow (throw on probe, catch picks the path) | gap | the catch handler's constant / the normal-path constant | `throw`, `move-exception`, try/catch around probes, custom `Exception` subclasses carrying state | `jadx`; evaluator must model handler tables | med-high |\n| 91 | Hook-framework detection (Frida, Xposed, Substrate, LSPosed) via introspection | gap (clean_device_scan covers ports/maps/packages) | value on the \"no hook\" path | `Thread.getStackTrace`/`Throwable.getStackTrace` class names, `/proc/self/task/*/comm` (`gum-js-loop`, `gmain`), `Modifier.isNative` on own methods, `de.robv.android.xposed` | `jadx`; `hook-framework-introspection-stubs` prebuild | high: next RESILIENCE theme |\n| 93 | Hardware key attestation `RootOfTrust` (cert chain extension OID 1.3.6.1.4.1.11129.2.1.17: verifiedBootKey, deviceLocked, verifiedBootState, verifiedBootHash, attestationChallenge) | gap (D22 title pun) | a field of the KeyDescription in a shipped DER/PEM cert, or the branch the app takes on `Verified`/`deviceLocked=true` | `getCertificateChain`, `KeyGenParameterSpec.setAttestationChallenge`, `1.3.6.1.4.1.11129.2.1.17`, `res/raw/*.der\\|*.pem`, `-----BEGIN CERTIFICATE` | `openssl x509 -in c.der -inform DER -text` [i]; `openssl asn1parse` [i]; `key-attestation-rootoftrust-parse` prebuild | high: title pun + Mastery repeats D22 |\n| 94 | Multi-signal root score / per-signal key (each probe contributes a bit, weight or fragment; forcing the aggregate `isRooted()=false` yields a decoy) | gap (D22 prompt \"multiple signals ... without globally patching success\") | value built from the clean result of EVERY signal (bitmask -> key, fragment concat, score threshold) | several probe methods feeding `or-int`/`shl-int`/`add-int` into one int, `StringBuilder.append` per probe, a `success`/`isRooted` field next to the vector | `root-signal-vector-key` prebuild; `clean_device_scan` [i] per probe | high |\n| 95 | Shell / process probes (`Runtime.exec(\"which su\")`, `ProcessBuilder(\"getprop\")`, `mount`, `getenforce`, `id`) | gap | the branch on the process output being empty / `Enforcing` / `ro` | `Ljava/lang/Runtime;->exec`, `ProcessBuilder`, `getInputStream`, `BufferedReader.readLine`, `/proc/mounts`, `/proc/self/mountinfo` | `process-exec-shell-probe-stubs` prebuild | med-high |\n| 92 | Biometric / local authentication bypass (MASVS-AUTH) | gap | `onAuthenticationSucceeded` body (CryptoObject null-tolerant) | `BiometricPrompt$AuthenticationCallback`, `FingerprintManager`, `KeyguardManager.isDeviceSecure`, `setUserAuthenticationRequired` | `jadx`; `biometric-auth-callback-eval` prebuild | med |\n\n## Recognition cues (worker quick-reference)\n\n```\n0. Always first: python3 -c \"from lib.android import extract_answer as e;print(e('x.apk'))\"   # puzzle->zip->dex->apktool/jadx\n   If it prints ANS-... and the prompt is the usual \"backend answer code\": submit. Do NOT chase 127.0.0.1:19090.\n1. unzip -l x.apk   -> map the entries:\n   assets/huntress_puzzle.json      puzzle codec; data already ANS-? done (D15 native, D19 reflection); new name -> data[:4] vs \"ANS-\"\n                                    data = an entry path (D20 `dynamic`: assets/payload.dex)? open THAT entry, recurse from 1.\n                                    int list beside data (D17 `indexed`, D5 `split`): r[order[i]] = data[i]; else gather\n   lib/<abi>/*.so                   strings -a | grep ANS- ; nm -D --defined-only ; no Java_* -> JNI_OnLoad/RegisterNatives\n                                    Java_*_native*(int) + *_accepts helper (D16 gate): objdump -d it; the value it returns\n                                    is the answer (D16: &arena_value = the .rodata ANS- literal; bypass len 65536)\n   lib/*/libapp.so + libflutter.so  Flutter: strings libapp.so; flutter_assets/kernel_blob.bin (debug = source text)\n   assets/index.android.bundle      RN: head -c8 | xxd; c61fbc03 = Hermes -> hbc-decompiler; else webcrack/js-beautify\n   assemblies/*.dll|*.blob, libmonodroid.so   Xamarin: XALZ = lz4 per-dll; then ilspycmd f.dll\n   libil2cpp.so + global-metadata.dat         Unity IL2CPP: strings global-metadata.dat | grep ANS- ; Managed/*.dll -> ilspycmd\n   assets/www/, cordova.js, capacitor.config  hybrid JS: grep -r in assets/www\n   assets/*.dex|*.jar|*.apk|*.zip|*.bin       dynamic code loading (D20: plain dex, ANS- const in `...payload.Module`):\n                                    strings -a it first; no dex/PK/ELF magic -> xor/known-plaintext unwrap (key from host dex);\n                                    >1 payload -> the one matching the host's pinned digest; >1 ANS- -> the member the host\n                                    names (`<entry>:<class>` string, `moduleContract`), never the first regex hit\n   libjiagu/libsecexe/libDexHelper.so          packer: payload is the encrypted asset; static decrypt or give up early\n   res/xml/network_security_config.xml        NSC: aapt dump xmltree x.apk res/xml/network_security_config.xml\n   resources.arsc                   aapt dump --values resources x.apk | grep -iE 'ans-|secret|key|flag|token'\n   *.db / shared_prefs/*.xml / *.ab sqlite3 f.db .dump ; .ab: dd bs=24 skip=1 | zlib-flate -uncompress | tar x\n   res/raw/*.bks|*.p12|*.pem        keystore: password is a dex string; keytool -list -v -storepass PW\n   google-services.json / firebase  key/URL itself may be the answer\n   base.apk + split_config.*.apk / manifest.json / toc.pb / BundleConfig.pb   split/XAPK/APKS/AAB: unzip inner, recurse\n   Payload/*.app/                   iOS: plistlib Info.plist; rz-bin -zz the Mach-O\n2. Plain-anywhere scan (incl. UTF-16 the zip scan misses):\n   for f in $(unzip -Z1 x.apk); do unzip -p x.apk \"$f\" | strings -a -el | grep -H --label=\"$f\" ANS-; done\n   7z l x.apk vs unzip -l x.apk differ -> zip tricks (dup entry / trailing data): binwalk x.apk\n3. Manifest (fast): aapt dump xmltree x.apk AndroidManifest.xml | grep -E \\\n   'exported|scheme|host|autoVerify|permission|debuggable|allowBackup|usesCleartext|networkSecurity|taskAffinity|launchMode|meta-data'\n   meta-data value= is a hiding spot (huntress.mechanic lives there). debuggable=true (D21) is a fact, not an answer.\n4. Dex triage: strings -a classes*.dex | grep -E 'DAY-|CODEC|ANS-|^[0-9A-F]{8,16}$' then map API hits to themes:\n   DexClassLoader/InMemoryDexClassLoader/moduleContract -> asset dex   SecretKeySpec/AES/Cipher -> static key decrypt\n   loadLibrary/RegisterNatives -> .so                     java/util/Random/setSeed/currentTimeMillis -> regenerate RNG\n   MessageDigest/PBKDF2 -> hash brute                     addJavascriptInterface/loadUrl/file:///android_asset -> assets html/js\n   Binder/$Stub/Messenger/onReceive -> IPC handler        CertificatePinner/sha256/ -> pins in code or NSC\n   su/magisk/goldfish/frida/TracerPid/isDebuggerConnected/debuggerGate (D21)/rootSignals (D22) -> clean_device_scan:\n   clean-path value PER SIGNAL; never force the aggregate isRooted()/success flag (D22 \"without globally patching\")\n   Class.forName/getDeclaredMethod -> reflection_scan     BuildConfig / R$string -> arsc / BuildConfig.java\n   Proxy/MethodHandles/invoke-custom -> real target; packed-switch in a loop / $SwitchMap$ -> flattened_cfg_scan\n   KeyStore.getInstance(\"BKS\"|\"PKCS12\") -> res/raw keystore + password string\n5. Read code only after 1-4: droidasc findrefs x.apk string <hit>; droidasc getclass x.apk <cls>; jadx -d w/jadx x.apk\n   (add --deobf for 1-2 letter class names). Strings split across constants: rebuild order from the method body.\n   String decryptors (D18 TT `EncryptedStrings.decryptByte`): dex_eval_scan, else jadx the helper, take the ARGS from\n   each call site, re-implement in py; unknown key/rolling scheme -> solve it from the ANS- known plaintext.\n   R8/decoys (D17): hint strings like \"follow b -> a and ignore field c\" name the chain; >1 ANS- candidate -> keep\n   the one appended before `proof=` in ChallengeActivity, never the first regex hit. Reflection/dispatch (D19 theme):\n   names may be encoded or picked by a key from the deep link/asset; evaluate only the invoked target, not its twins.\n   lib scanners for code-side answers (not in extract_answer): renamed_chain_scan, proof_flow_scan, dex_eval_scan,\n   reflection_scan, mapping_restore_scan, signing_block_scan, zip_structure_scan  (all lib.android, take apk path)\n6. Native, if no literal: rizin -A -qc 'iE; izz~ANS; afl' f.so ; pdf @ sym.Java_... ; xor loops -> py capstone/unicorn.\n7. Validate: candidate must fullmatch ^ANS-[0-9A-F]{16}$ (uppercase). Two sources (asset + .so) agreeing = submit.\n8. Mastery: each set can be a different day's fixture; decode every APK on its own; loop over all answer_ids (3/5/6).\n```\n\n## Readiness gaps\n\nPriority 1 = plausible within ~3 days. \"prebuild\" = pure-python extractor in `lib/android.py` style that races in\n`solve.py`. \"tool\" = install. \"note\" = doc/prompt change. Already built (prebuild-state ok, dropped from the list):\naab-proto-manifest-parse, ans-prefix-numeric-compose, anti-debug-state-machine-clean-path, apk-signing-block-payload,\nasset-cipher-dex-loader, asset-db-prefs-backup, attestation-jws-claims, binder-ontransact-code-map,\nbroadcast-receiver-action-map, cdex-vdex-string-pool, cert-and-signing-facts, cert-pin-and-nsc-facts,\nclassloader-shadow-resolve, clean-device-env-stubs, custom-alphabet-decode, dalvik-mini-interpreter,\ndart-snapshot-string-pool, decode-any-chain-peel, decrypt-call-site-args-eval, dex-bytecode-integrity-gate,\ndex-gated-branch-consts, dex-native-call-args, dex-native-split-assembly, dex-slack-and-header-anomaly,\ndex-string-decrypt-arrays, dispatch-key-resolve, emulator-telephony-sensor-stubs, entry-reachable-callgraph-rank,\nenum-switchmap-state-resolve, exception-driven-control-flow, flattened-cfg-switch-eval, hermes-hbc-string-table,\nhook-framework-introspection-stubs, identifier-collision-resolve, identity-derived-key, il2cpp-metadata-literals,\nintegrity-derived-key, java-serialized-object-parse, jni-export-return-trace, jni-gate-bypass-input,\njni-reflection-callback, jwt-token-decode-verify, known-string-obfuscator-signatures,\nkotlin-metadata-names-and-coroutines, messagedigest-derived-answer, module-contract-member-eval, multi-abi-arm-native,\nmulti-stage-loader-recurse, native-gated-branch-read, native-init-array-decrypt, native-libc-probe-stubs-emulate,\nnative-payload-system-load, native-so-emulate-export, native-stack-string, nested-container-recurse,\nopaque-predicate-dead-branch, payload-digest-pinned-select, payload-magic-known-plaintext-unwrap,\npermutation-transposition-family, proguard-mapping-restore, proof-flow-candidate-ranking, protobuf-asset-wire-decode,\nproxy-methodhandle-invokecustom, puzzle-entry-pointer-follow, puzzle-indexed-and-perm-fields, r8-renamed-chain-follow,\nreflection-name-resolve, registernatives-table, resource-id-const-resolve, rolling-xor-keystream-family,\nsqlcipher-asset-decrypt, static-key-cipher-decode, timing-and-debug-flag-probe-stubs, tiny-bytecode-vm-interpret,\nutf16-string-pool-scan, v1-manifest-digest-verify, webview-asset-js-scan, xamarin-xalz-blob-unpack,\nzip-structure-anomaly-scan.\nForecast after D22: the arc is walking MASVS-RESILIENCE one control per day (D21 anti-debug, D22 root). Next most likely:\nemulator detection, hook/Frida detection, tamper/installer/signature checks, attestation (key attestation `RootOfTrust`,\nPlay Integrity), then obfuscation capstones. Code-side gates have never shipped (TT dex only names the mechanic:\n`debuggerGate`, `rootSignals`); the gaps below harden the clean-device evaluator for the day one does.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"id\": \"root-signal-vector-key\", \"concept\": \"multi-signal root detection where each probe contributes a bit/weight/fragment and the answer is derived from the whole clean vector (rows 47, 94)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D22 prompt: 'Model and bypass multiple synthetic root signals without globally patching success'; TT dex string `rootSignals`. Expected real version: N probe methods (su paths, Build.TAGS test-keys, magisk/superuser packages, ro.debuggable/ro.secure, rw /system mount, which su, SELinux) each returning boolean/int; results combined by or-int/shl-int into a mask, summed into a score vs threshold, or appended as fragments; the mask/score keys an xor/hash that yields the ANS- value, so forcing isRooted()/success=true at the aggregate gives a DECOY. Build `root_signal_scan(apk)`: locate probe methods (methods whose bodies hit the clean_device_scan probe table), evaluate each with clean retail-phone answers through the Dalvik evaluator, then evaluate the combiner method with those per-signal results (not with a forced aggregate). Report the clean-vector value first; also report (labelled, demoted) the value from a forced-success path so the solver can tell them apart. Handle signals stored in a boolean[]/int[]/BitSet/EnumSet/Map<String,Boolean>. Budget <0.8 s, never raise.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"probe-arg-resolve-before-stub\", \"concept\": \"root/emulator probe arguments built at runtime (split, reversed, xor'd paths and package names) so the stub must see the computed string (rows 47, 48, 94)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"clean_device_scan keys its answers on literal strings (`/system/xbin/su`, `com.topjohnwu.magisk`, `test-keys`). A real root gate hides them: `new File(dec(\\\"...\\\")).exists()`, `\\\"/sys\\\"+\\\"tem/\\\"+\\\"bin/su\\\"`, reversed `us/nib/metsys/`, char arrays, base64. Make every probe stub match on the EVALUATED argument (after the evaluator runs the decoder/StringBuilder) and normalise it (collapse //, strip trailing /, casefold) before lookup; unknown paths under /system,/sbin,/su,/data/local,/data/adb,/cache -> non-existent; unknown package names containing magisk/supersu/kingroot/xposed/lsposed/zygisk/frida -> NameNotFoundException. Log each (probe, resolved arg, stub answer) so the worker can audit. Synthetic test: path assembled from 3 fragments and a 1-byte xor.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"process-exec-shell-probe-stubs\", \"concept\": \"Runtime.exec / ProcessBuilder shell probes with stubbed process I/O (row 95)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Root checks often run `which su`, `su -c id`, `getprop ro.build.tags`, `getprop ro.debuggable`, `mount`, `getenforce`, `id`, `ls /data/adb`. Stub in the Dalvik evaluator: Runtime.getRuntime().exec(String|String[]) and new ProcessBuilder(..).start() -> a fake Process whose getInputStream yields clean output per command (which su -> '' ; su -> IOException 'Cannot run program'; getprop ro.build.tags -> 'release-keys'; ro.debuggable -> '0'; ro.secure -> '1'; getenforce -> 'Enforcing'; id -> 'uid=10123(u0_a123) gid=10123'; mount / cat /proc/mounts -> '/dev/block/dm-0 /system ext4 ro,seclabel,relatime 0 0' lines, no magisk/tmpfs on /system), waitFor/exitValue -> 1 for which/su, 0 otherwise; InputStreamReader/BufferedReader.readLine/Scanner/readText over it; File('/proc/mounts'|'/proc/self/mountinfo') reads -> same clean text. Command arg resolved via probe-arg-resolve-before-stub.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"key-attestation-rootoftrust-parse\", \"concept\": \"Android hardware key attestation: parse the KeyDescription / RootOfTrust extension from shipped certs (row 93)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D22's title 'Root of Trust' is the ASN.1 RootOfTrust in key attestation (OID 1.3.6.1.4.1.11129.2.1.17 KeyDescription -> teeEnforced/softwareEnforced AuthorizationList tag [704] rootOfTrust = SEQUENCE{verifiedBootKey OCTET STRING, deviceLocked BOOLEAN, verifiedBootState ENUM(0 Verified,1 SelfSigned,2 Unverified,3 Failed), verifiedBootHash OCTET STRING}; also attestationChallenge, attestationSecurityLevel, attestationApplicationId [709] with package name + signature digests, osVersion [705], osPatchLevel [706]). Build `key_attestation_scan(apk)`: find DER/PEM certs and chains in any entry (assets/res/raw/META-INF/puzzle JSON base64 fields; `-----BEGIN CERTIFICATE`, 30 82 DER), parse with a minimal pure-python DER walker (no subprocess), extract the extension, decode the AuthorizationList, report all fields; ANS- regex on challenge/octet strings (also hex/ASCII of verifiedBootHash); compare attestationApplicationId signature digest to signing_certs(apk) and verifiedBootState to the dex constants the app compares. Clean = Verified + deviceLocked true.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"installer-source-and-tamper-probe-stubs\", \"concept\": \"anti-tamper / repackaging probes: installer source, signature, debuggable flag, dex CRC (rows 49, 50)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"After root/emulator/hook the arc names tamper checks. Extend the clean-device probe table: PackageManager.getInstallerPackageName / getInstallSourceInfo().getInstallingPackageName / getInitiatingPackageName -> 'com.android.vending'; getPackageInfo(own, GET_SIGNATURES|GET_SIGNING_CERTIFICATES).signatures/signingInfo.getApkContentsSigners -> the APK's REAL v1/v2 cert bytes from signing_certs(apk) (so hashCode/MessageDigest comparisons evaluate on the true digest); ApplicationInfo.flags FLAG_DEBUGGABLE bit from the manifest; ApplicationInfo.sourceDir/publicSourceDir -> '/data/app/<pkg>-1/base.apk'; ZipFile(sourceDir).getEntry('classes.dex').getCrc() -> the real CRC from the APK; Context.getPackageCodePath likewise. Integrate with dex_integrity_gate_scan / integrity_key_scan (built) so a digest-keyed answer uses real bytes. Report the value on the untampered path.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"worker-cue-inline\", \"concept\": \"unseen-theme routing\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Inline the 'Recognition cues' block above into the mobile worker prompt (skills/huntress-ctf mobile skill) so an unseen container (Flutter/RN/Xamarin/asset dex) is routed in 1-2 turns; add step 2's UTF-16 scan to triage.md pre-extraction.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"native-system-property-and-mounts-stubs\", \"concept\": \"native root/emulator probes via __system_property_get, popen and /proc/self/mounts inside the .so (rows 66, 95)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"native-libc-probe-stubs-emulate (built) covers ptrace/TracerPid/access/stat. Add unicorn import stubs: __system_property_get(name, buf) / __system_property_find + __system_property_read(_callback) -> clean values (ro.build.tags release-keys, ro.debuggable 0, ro.secure 1, ro.boot.verifiedbootstate green, ro.boot.flash.locked 1, ro.kernel.qemu '', ro.hardware a real SoC); popen/pclose + fgets for 'which su'/'getprop'/'mount' -> clean text; fopen('/proc/self/mounts'|'/proc/mounts'|'/proc/self/mountinfo') -> lines without magisk/tmpfs-on-/system/overlay; opendir/readdir on /data/adb, /sbin -> empty; dlopen of libmagisk/libfrida -> NULL. Same import resolution path (pyelftools .rela.plt), x86_64 then arm64.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"native-inline-syscall-stubs\", \"concept\": \"native probes issuing raw syscalls (svc #0 / syscall instruction) to bypass libc hooks\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Hardened root/anti-hook checks call openat/faccessat/readlinkat/newfstatat/ptrace/getppid directly via `syscall` (x86_64) or `svc #0` (arm64) so Frida libc hooks miss them. In the unicorn runner, hook UC_HOOK_INSN syscall (x86_64) / UC_HOOK_INTR (arm64), dispatch on rax/x8 number (x86_64: openat 257, faccessat 269, newfstatat 262, readlinkat 267, read 0, close 3, ptrace 101, getppid 110; arm64: openat 56, faccessat 48, newfstatat 79, readlinkat 78, read 63, close 57, ptrace 117, getppid 173) and answer from the same clean filesystem/proc model as the libc stubs (ENOENT for su paths, fake fd for /proc/self/status with TracerPid 0). Test with a tiny hand-assembled .so.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"play-integrity-verdict-select\", \"concept\": \"Play Integrity / SafetyNet verdict JSON drives the branch: pick the value for the strongest clean verdict (row 87)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"attestation-jws-claims (built) decodes tokens. Add verdict semantics: parse decoded payloads or plain JSON assets with requestDetails{requestPackageName, nonce, timestampMillis}, appIntegrity{appRecognitionVerdict PLAY_RECOGNIZED|UNRECOGNIZED_VERSION|UNEVALUATED, packageName, certificateSha256Digest[], versionCode}, deviceIntegrity{deviceRecognitionVerdict [MEETS_BASIC_INTEGRITY, MEETS_DEVICE_INTEGRITY, MEETS_STRONG_INTEGRITY, MEETS_VIRTUAL_INTEGRITY]}, accountDetails{appLicensingVerdict LICENSED}, legacy SafetyNet ctsProfileMatch/basicIntegrity/evaluationType HARDWARE_BACKED. When several verdict blobs or dex branches exist, rank the one with PLAY_RECOGNIZED + MEETS_DEVICE/STRONG_INTEGRITY + LICENSED + certificateSha256Digest equal to signing_certs(apk) + nonce matching the host's computed nonce; report the ANS- value tied to it; demote others as decoys.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"biometric-auth-callback-eval\", \"concept\": \"MASVS-AUTH biometric / local auth bypass: the success callback holds the secret (row 92)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Untouched MASVS group. Find classes extending androidx.biometric.BiometricPrompt$AuthenticationCallback, android.hardware.biometrics.BiometricPrompt$AuthenticationCallback or FingerprintManager(Compat)$AuthenticationCallback, KeyguardManager.createConfirmDeviceCredentialIntent + onActivityResult(RESULT_OK). Evaluate onAuthenticationSucceeded(result) with a result whose getCryptoObject() returns null (event-bound bypass) AND with a CryptoObject wrapping a stub Cipher (doFinal = identity) -- report both values labelled; evaluate onActivityResult with resultCode -1. Also flag `setUserAuthenticationRequired(false)` / missing `setInvalidatedByBiometricEnrollment`. ANS- regex on the results; demote values reached only on onAuthenticationFailed/onAuthenticationError.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"pyxamstore\", \"concept\": \"Xamarin assemblies.blob / XALZ (row 55)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"pip: `uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python pyxamstore` (or github jakev/pyxamstore). Then `pyxamstore unpack -d assemblies/` and ilspycmd. Also small prebuild: XALZ header (magic, index, size) + lz4.block decompress (lz4 in venv).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"apkid\", \"concept\": \"packer / obfuscator / anti-VM identification (rows 44-48)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"pip: `uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python apkid` (needs yara-python, already OK). `apkid -j x.apk` names packers, obfuscators and anti-debug in one call: a fast routing cue for an unseen theme.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"bundletool\", \"concept\": \"AAB / APKS packaging (row 58)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github release jar google/bundletool (bundletool-all-1.17.x.jar) into tools/bundletool + bin shim. `bundletool dump manifest --bundle x.aab`, `bundletool build-apks --mode=universal`. AAB manifests are protobuf, so aapt dump xmltree fails on them.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"whitebox-table-cipher-eval\", \"concept\": \"white-box / table-driven cipher (lookup-table AES or byte S-box chains) as an obfuscation capstone\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"After VM/flattening the next obfuscation step is table-based crypto with the key folded into large static arrays (int[256]/byte[4096] T-boxes, Tyi tables, or chained byte S-boxes) in dex <clinit> or .so .rodata. Don't recover the key: evaluate the table walk. Dex: dex_array_scan to pull the arrays, then run the decrypt method in the Dalvik evaluator with arrays preloaded (raise its step budget for 10-16 rounds of aget/xor); .so: unicorn-run the export over .rodata tables. Fallback: if the method is a pure byte-wise S-box chain, compose the tables in python and invert via the ANS- known plaintext. Budget <0.8 s.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ios-ipa-readiness\", \"concept\": \"iOS IPA (row 64)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Lane is named mobile-android; if an .ipa ever ships: unzip Payload/, plistlib for Info.plist and binary plists, rz-bin -zz / lief for Mach-O strings, ipsw (github blacktop/ipsw release) for class-dump. Nothing to prebuild now.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"il2cppdumper\", \"concept\": \"Unity IL2CPP (row 56)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github release Perfare/Il2CppDumper (or SamboyCoding/Cpp2IL) into tools/; run with bin/dotnet. Only if a Unity fixture ever ships.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"blutter\", \"concept\": \"Flutter Dart AOT (row 52)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github worawit/blutter (python3 blutter.py <lib dir> <out>; builds per Dart version with cmake/ninja + fetches the Dart SDK, slow first run; arm64 only). Alt: pip reflutter (needs repack + device: low value). Plain strings on libapp.so cover literal answers.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"abe\", \"concept\": \"encrypted Android backup (row 16)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github release nelenkov/android-backup-extractor (abe.jar): `java -jar abe.jar unpack b.ab b.tar [pw]`. Needed only for encrypted .ab (PBKDF2+AES); unencrypted is zlib-flate.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"frida-tools\", \"concept\": \"dynamic instrumentation / root and frida checks (rows 47, 48)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"pip frida-tools / objection. Low value: no Android device or emulator here (adb present, no target), and every answer so far was static. Keep the rule: read the gated branch statically.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"standalone-baksmali\", \"concept\": \"smali-level reading / patching (row 51)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"Link tools/dex2jar/d2j-baksmali.sh + d2j-smali.sh into bin/ (already on disk), or github google/smali release. apktool d already emits smali, so cosmetic.\"}\n]\n```","numLines":190,"startLine":80,"totalLines":270}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Pqj3ojazubKcTK6GKmUQv5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
