 scan, dex strings incl. multidex, apktool/jadx), then `strings -a classes*.dex assets/* lib/*/*.so \\| grep ANS-` |","-| Need theme, component, scheme, exported flags | `droidasc getmanifest x.apk`; `aapt dump xmltree x.apk AndroidManifest.xml`; `lib.android.manifest_facts(apk)` |","-| 1-letter classes, hint \"follow b -> a and ignore field c\", `decoy` (d17) | asset first. If the answer leaves it: `jadx --deobf`, follow the chain the hint names; prefer the value that flows into `proof=` |","-| `EncryptedStrings`/`decryptByte` (d18), `ReflectionMaze`/`dispatch` (d19) | asset first. Code-side: `dex_eval_scan` / `reflection_scan`, then `proof_flow_scan` to pick the value that reaches `proof=` |","-| Anti-debug theme: `debuggerGate`, `anti_debug`, manifest `debuggable=true` (d21); later maybe `isDebuggerConnected`, `TracerPid`, `ptrace`, clock deltas | asset first (d21: plain `reverse`, no probe code at all). If code gates the value: `clean_device_scan` (probes answer as a clean retail device), `flattened_cfg_scan` for a `while/switch(state)` loop; take the clean-path value, never run it |","-| Root theme: `rootSignals`, `root_detection`, class `RootOfTrust`, \"multiple root signals\" (d22); later maybe `su` paths, `test-keys`, `magisk`, `Runtime.exec(\"which su\")`, attestation certs | asset first (d22: plain `base64`, no probe code). If code gates the value: `clean_device_scan` per signal (each probe answered as a retail phone), keep the clean-path value; never force the aggregate `isRooted()`/success flag (\"without globally patching success\" = the value may be built from the per-signal results) |","-| Handler logic (URL, extras, constants) | `droidasc findrefs x.apk string <scheme or URL>`, `droidasc getclass x.apk <pkg>.ChallengeActivity`; `jadx -d work/jadx x.apk` |","-| Loopback `127.0.0.1:19090` in the code | do NOT chase it: device-local. The answer is static |","-| Prompt demands a live action (\"replay the session\" d8, \"exploit a CA\" d9, \"challenge-signed\" d20) | still static: `unzip -l` for pcap/HAR/cert/extra dex first. d20's \"signed\" module had no verify code; the v1 `MANIFEST.MF` merely lists its digest |","-| Backup theme with a real `.ab` file (not seen) | 24-byte header + zlib: `dd bs=24 skip=1 \\| zlib-flate -uncompress \\| tar x` |","-| Mastery `delivery N: foo_mastery_0N.apk` | strip the prefix (`lib.common.find_artifact`). Ids `setN.answer`; each set may be another day's fixture |","+| `*.apk`, answer `ANS- + 16 uppercase hex` | `unzip -p x.apk assets/huntress_puzzle.json` (triage.md pre-extracts + prints it) |","+| puzzle v1 `{\"codec\":..,\"data\":..}` | decode per codec (list below); fullmatch `^ANS-[0-9A-F]{16}$` before submitting |","+| **puzzle v2 `\"codec\":\"analysis\"`, no `data`** (d23) | answer = `Release.code(ctx)`. Fast manual path: `jadx -q -d j x.apk`; copy non-Activity sources; stub `package android.content; public class Context {}`; `Main` prints `Release.code(null)`; `javac` + `java`. Or port the ~6 static long fns to python (mask 2^64, `>>>` = logical) |","+| v2 chain calls a `native` method (d23 d15 set `nativeShare(long)`) | `objdump -d -M intel lib/*/libarena.so` the export (~10 insns of movabs/add/xor/imul/rol) and port to python, or unicorn-emulate it. Do NOT `ctypes.CDLL` the artifact on the host |","+| `Probe.s1/s2/s3(a,b,c,d)` loops | 12-bit inverse search: smallest i<4096 with f(i)==d, else -1. Pure, cheap: just evaluate |","+| `data` is a path (`assets/payload.dex`, d20) | `unzip -p x.apk assets/payload.dex \\| strings -a \\| grep ANS-`; no dex magic -> known-plaintext unwrap |","+| int list next to `data` (d17 `indexed`, d5 `split`) | `order[i]` = OUTPUT slot of `data[i]`: `r[order[i]] = data[i]` |","+| Unknown v1 codec name | `data` already `ANS-`? An entry name? Else `data[:4]` vs `ANS-`: constant diff = shift, constant XOR = key |","+| `lib/<abi>/*.so` | `strings -a \\| grep ANS-`, `nm -D --defined-only`; d16 gate `nativeEvidence(int)`: `objdump -d` the checker (65536) |","+| Nothing decodes | `lib.android.extract_answer`, then `strings -a classes*.dex assets/* lib/*/*.so \\| grep ANS-` |","+| Theme stubs (d17-d22: `a`/decoy, `decryptByte`, `dispatch`, `debuggerGate`, `rootSignals`) | asset first. Code-side: `dex_eval_scan`/`reflection_scan`/`clean_device_scan`, then `proof_flow_scan` to keep the value reaching `proof=` |","+| Hook/instrumentation theme (d23 `hook_detection`, prompt \"real signals vs generated false positives\") | v2 chain; the gate fn is pure arithmetic over probe results; look-alike `seal*`/`K*` members nobody calls are the decoys |","+| Loopback `127.0.0.1:19090` | do NOT chase it: device-local. The answer is static |","+| Prompt demands a live action (d8 \"replay\", d9 \"exploit CA\", d20 \"signed\") | still static: `unzip -l` for extra entries first |","+| Mastery `delivery N: foo_mastery_0N.apk` | strip the prefix (`lib.common.find_artifact`); ids `setN.answer`; each set may be another day AND another schema |"," ","-Puzzle codecs seen (`schema: huntress.mobile.puzzle.v1`):","-- `plain`, `native` (d15-d16, duplicated in the `.so`), `reflection` (d19): `data` is the answer.","-- `dynamic` (d20): `data` = zip entry path; read the entry, `ANS-` literal inside the dex (`puzzle_candidates` yields the","-  path string itself, so the solver's `raw_entry_scan` fallback found it -- follow the pointer explicitly).","-- `reverse` (d2, d8, d21); `base64` (d3, d9, d13, d22); `hex` (d6, d12).","-- `caesar` (d7, d14): `{data, key:int}`, `chr(ord(c) - key)` over EVERY char (digits and `-` too, `KX]7` key 10 -> `ANS-`);","-  a letters-only ROT is wrong. Derive the sign from `data[:4]` vs `ANS-`.","-- `xor` (d4, d11, d18): base64 data, XOR every byte with int `key` (0-255).","-- `split` (d5, d10): `parts[]` + `order[]`, `order[i]` = OUTPUT SLOT of `parts[i]`. Try both readings, keep the `ANS-` one.","-- `indexed` (d17): 20 chars + `order[20]`, `r[order[i]] = data[i]` (`permutation_candidates` tries scatter + gather).","-- `lib.android.decode_payload` / `puzzle_candidates(apk)` / `decode_any` (base32, rot13, `lib.decode.peel`) cover these.","-  Code-side scanners (call yourself; not in `extract_answer`): `renamed_chain_scan`, `proof_flow_scan`, `dex_eval_scan`,","-  `reflection_scan`, `mapping_restore_scan`, `signing_block_scan`, `zip_structure_scan`, `integrity_key_scan`.","+Puzzle codecs seen (v1): `plain`, `native` (d15-d16), `reflection` (d19) = plaintext; `dynamic` (d20) = entry path;","+`reverse` (d2, d8, d21); `base64` (d3, d9, d13, d22); `hex` (d6, d12); `caesar` (d7, d14: `chr(ord(c)-key)` over EVERY","+char, sign from `data[:4]`); `xor` (d4, d11, d18, d23 single: base64 + int key 0-255); `split` (d5, d10: `parts[]` +","+`order[]`); `indexed` (d17). v2: `analysis` (d23). `lib.android.decode_payload` / `puzzle_candidates` / `decode_any`","+cover v1. Code-side: `bytecode_vm_scan` (`_DxVM`, bigger budget) reproduced the d23 TT value but resolved only 2 of","+8 v2 APKs; also `renamed_chain_scan`, `proof_flow_scan`, `dex_eval_scan`, `reflection_scan`, `ans_compose_scan`","+(on v2 it returns ANS-shaped DECOYS from the dead mixers -- never submit its first hit)."," "," ## Day by day"," ","-**Days 1-6** (same 6-entry fixture, all first try): d1 Exported Trust `plain` (~5.4 min, ~4 min lost probing","-`127.0.0.1:19090`); d2 Deep Link Drift `reverse` (33 s); d3 Intent Injection `base64` (18 s); d4 Pending Intent Relay","-`xor` (77 s); d5 Backup Spill `split` -- `order[i]` = output slot (27 s); d6 Provider Paths `hex` (~3 min, 2.3 min lost on","-the loopback).","+**Days 1-6** (all first try): d1 Exported Trust `plain` (~5.4 min, ~4 min lost on the loopback); d2 Deep Link Drift","+`reverse`; d3 Intent Injection `base64`; d4 Pending Intent Relay `xor`; d5 Backup Spill `split` (`order[i]` = output","+slot); d6 Provider Paths `hex` (2.3 min lost on the loopback)."," ","-**Days 7-15** (theme stubs never needed; 0 wrong, TT/Mastery 0.8-3.5 s in-window): d7 WebView Bridge new `caesar`; d8","-Cleartext Session `reverse`; d9 Trust Everyone `base64`; d10 Network Config Split `split` (8-entry + NSC); d11 Local","-Secrets `xor`; d12 SQLite Assumptions `hex`; d13 Keystore Misuse `base64`; d14 Predictable Crypto `caesar` (json-load the","-`\\\\`/`<` escapes). d15 Native Library Secrets: first `libarena.so` (answer literal in `.rodata`), codec `native` =","-plaintext; first MIXED-DAY Mastery.","+**Days 7-15** (0 wrong, TT/Mastery 0.8-3.5 s): d7 WebView Bridge NEW `caesar`; d8 Cleartext `reverse`; d9 Trust","+Everyone `base64`; d10 Network Config Split `split` (8-entry + NSC); d11 Local Secrets `xor`; d12 SQLite `hex`; d13","+Keystore `base64`; d14 Predictable Crypto `caesar` (json-load escapes). d15 Native Library Secrets: first `libarena.so`","+(literal in `.rodata`), codec `native`; first MIXED-DAY Mastery."," ","-**Days 16-19** (asset held the answer; 0 wrong; carried-over solver CORRECT in ~2-25 s): d16 JNI Boundary, `native`; TT","-`.so` added the `nativeEvidence(int)` gate (65536). d17 Name Collapse, NEW `indexed` (race probe silent, duel worker added","-the decoder -> ~24.5 s); TT hint `follow b -> a and ignore field c`. d18 Encrypted Strings, `xor` (3rd time); TT","-`decryptByte`. d19 Reflection Maze, NEW `reflection` = plaintext; no reflection API in any dex; TT `dispatch`.","+**Days 16-22** (asset held the answer; 0 wrong; carried-over solver CORRECT in ~2-25 s): d16 JNI Boundary `native`, TT","+`.so` gate (65536). d17 Name Collapse NEW `indexed`, TT hint `follow b -> a and ignore field c`. d18 Encrypted Strings","+`xor`, TT `decryptByte`. d19 Reflection Maze NEW `reflection` = plaintext. d20 Loaded Later NEW `dynamic`: `data` =","+entry path, answer a const in `assets/payload.dex` class `...payload.Module`. d21 Debug Me If You Can `reverse`,","+`debuggable=true`, no probe code. d22 Root of Trust `base64`, no probe code; first 6-set Mastery; title pun = key","+attestation ASN.1 `RootOfTrust`."," ","-**Day 20 — Loaded Later** (`dynamic_dex`): 7-entry APK + `assets/payload.dex` (508 B plain dex). NEW codec `dynamic`:","-`data` = the ENTRY PATH; answer = the only `ANS-` const in `com.huntress.arena.payload.Module`. No ClassLoader/verify","-code (\"challenge-signed\" was narrative); TT host dex added `moduleContract` + `<entry>:<class>`. Generic `answer()` was","-silent (pointer string); `raw_entry_scan` found it. CORRECT ~8.4 s; TT 3.06 s, Mastery 5.19 s.","+**Day 23 — Hook Line and Signal** (`CONTROL=\"hook_detection\"`, `STRUCTURAL=\"hook and instrumentation detection\"`; prompt","+\"Separate real instrumentation signals from generated false positives.\")","+- Single: plain v1 6-entry fixture (12704 B, dex 2604 B), `{\"codec\":\"xor\",\"data\":\"<b64>\",\"key\":81}`. Race probe","+  CORRECT 22.4 s after start (13:00:14.9Z -> 13:00:37.3Z).","+- TT: SAME 12704 B size but puzzle **v2 `analysis`**, dex 5684 B, no `ANS-` literal anywhere. jadx shows:","+  `Release.token() = HookScan.mixPatcheb(Util.scanSignal61(Util.mixTrampoline79(<const long>)))`; `scanSignal61` xors","+  in three `Probe.s3/s3/s2(...)` results times constants plus `HookLineAndSignal.instrumentationSignals(a,b,c)*K`;","+  `Release.code` = `\"ANS-%016X\"` of `Util.finTrampoline2d(Mix.f1(token())) ^ K`. ChallengeActivity only calls `code`","+  if the `answer` extra equalsIgnoreCase `Release.proof` (= `Long.toHexString(token())`), then puts `code` in `proof=`.","+  Unreferenced look-alikes (`TrampolineMap.sealTrampolinec7`, `Util.sealHook30`, `HookScan.sealHook1e`, `KHook59`,","+  `KPatchea`) are the \"generated false positives\". Live worker: jadx -> python port of 6 fns -> CORRECT 94.5 s after","+  start (no clock).","+- Mastery: 7 sets (d02, d06, d10, d14, d15, d22, d23), ALL v2. Live worker: jadx all 7, `javac` the non-Activity","+  sources against a 1-line `android.content.Context` stub, one `Main` per set printing `Release.proof(null)` +","+  `Release.code(null)` -> 6 accepted at ~97 s; d15 set: `nativeShare(long)` -> Java stub printed the native input,","+  native result computed, re-run -> CORRECT ~2.0 min after start. (The worker called the export via `ctypes.CDLL` on the","+  host -- it worked because the fn is pure arithmetic, but it runs untrusted code: emulate or port instead.)","+- Solver: the carried-over solver was SILENT on every v2 APK (the harness then probed with `ANS-0123456789ABCDEF`,","+  marked incorrect). Generalize workers found `lib.android.bytecode_vm_scan` reproduces the TT value with a raised step","+  budget but resolves only 2 of 8 v2 APKs (Context param stored in a static, array ops, native call); they were cut off","+  at CORRECT, so **solve.py still has no v2 path** -- a v2 evaluator is tomorrow's top prebuild.","+- GM spelling unchanged: `answer` / `setN.answer`, `exact`. 0 wrong answers from workers."," ","-**Day 21 — Debug Me If You Can** (`anti_debug`): plain 6-entry fixture, codec back to `reverse`; the ONLY manifest with","-`android:debuggable=\"true\"`. No `Debug`/`TracerPid`/clock API, no state loop -- \"neutralize a clean-room anti-debug state","-machine\" was narrative. TT dex added `debuggerGate` + `STRUCTURAL`. Race probe CORRECT ~3.1 s; TT 2.23 s, Mastery 2.10 s.","-","-**Day 22 — Root of Trust** (manifest `huntress.mechanic`=`synthetic root detection`, dex `DAY-22:root_detection:synthetic","-root detection`, class `RootOfTrust`, deep link `huntress22://root-of-trust/unlock`; prompt \"Model and bypass multiple","-synthetic root signals without globally patching success.\")","-- Artifact: plain 6-entry fixture (12704 B, dex 2576 B, `debuggable` false), puzzle `{\"codec\":\"base64\",\"data\":\"<b64 of","-  ANS-...>\"}` -- 4th `base64` day. No root probe code in any dex: no `File.exists`, `Build.TAGS`, `Runtime.exec`, su/","-  magisk/test-keys strings. \"Multiple signals\" and \"without globally patching success\" were narrative.","-- TT + today's Mastery set: dex 2648 B, drops the `DAY-22` tag and `describe`, adds `STRUCTURAL`, `rootSignals`,","-  `synthetic root detection`. Same `base64` codec.","-- Mastery: FIRST 6-set bundle (`set1..set6.answer`): d01 plain, d07 caesar, d12 hex, d13 base64, d17 indexed, d22","-  base64. The carried-over solver loops answer_ids, so the extra set cost nothing.","-- Key insight: none needed -- the asset held the answer; the d16-d22 \"TT dex names the mechanic\" pattern held again.","-  Title pun to remember: Android KEY ATTESTATION has an ASN.1 `RootOfTrust` (verifiedBootKey, deviceLocked,","-  verifiedBootState, verifiedBootHash) -- if attestation certs ever ship, that is where to look.","-- Time: race probe CORRECT 9.2 s after start (13:00:11.98Z -> 13:00:21.17Z); the LLM worker only confirmed. TT in-window","-  1.48 s (solve 0.02 s); Mastery 6 sets in-window 1.65 s (solve 0.05 s). `no_clock: true` (d19-d22). All first try, 0","-  wrong. GM spelling unchanged: `answer` / `setN.answer`, `exact`.","-"," ## GM answer conventions learned","-- One field, `answer`. Single solve and TT use id `answer`; Mastery uses `setN.answer` (3, 5 or 6 sets), one APK per set.","-- Format is `ANS-` + exactly 16 UPPERCASE hex, normalization `exact`. Uppercase the hex after decoding, no whitespace.","-- No mobile answer has ever been rejected (zero wrong submissions on days 1-22). The GM accepts the statically recovered","-  value as the \"backend evidence code\" even though the prompt says \"Submit only the exact backend answer code\".","-- Mastery feedback is per set: `{\"result\":\"accepted\",\"remaining\":N}` after each set, then `CORRECT` on the last. An","-  empty submit after the deadline returns `expired`.","-- Prompt boilerplate: \"For case MOB-NN-<10 hex> in package com.huntress.mobile.dNN.v<12 hex>\". In Mastery the text is","-  today's and the case ref may not match the APK (d16). Neither was ever needed for the answer.","+- One field, `answer`. Single solve and TT use id `answer`; Mastery uses `setN.answer` (3, 5, 6 or 7 sets).","+- Format `ANS-` + exactly 16 UPPERCASE hex, normalization `exact`. v2 code already emits uppercase via the hex table.","+- No worker-derived mobile answer has ever been rejected (d1-d23). Only harness placeholders from a silent solver were.","+- Mastery feedback per set: `{\"result\":\"accepted\",\"remaining\":N,\"accepted_ids\":[..]}`, then `CORRECT` on the last.","+- Prompt boilerplate: \"For case MOB-NN-<10 hex> in package com.huntress.mobile.dNN.v<12 hex>\". Never needed."," "," ## Pitfalls that cost time","-- **Chasing the loopback backend** was the only recurring time sink: ~4 min (d1), ~30 s (d4), ~2.3 min (d6).","-  `127.0.0.1:19090` is the phone's own loopback. If a static value matches the answer_format, submit it.","-- **Taking `data` at face value** (d20): `data` was an entry path, not a value. Never submit or \"decode\" a string that","-  names a zip entry; open the entry. Always fullmatch the ANS regex on the final value.","-- **Assuming \"today's codec\" in Mastery** (d15+): sets come from older days with different codecs and extra entries.","-- **Reaching for Ghidra on a native-lib theme** (d15-d16): the `.so` is ~14 KB, unstripped, the answer a literal. Use","-  `strings`/`nm`, then `objdump -d` of the one `Java_*` export. Same for d20's payload: `strings` before `jadx`.","-- **Trusting the question's case ref in Mastery** (d16): it can name a different day/case than the APK it points at.","-- **New codec, generic solver silent** (d17 `indexed`, ~20 s lost): when the JSON has an unknown codec, write the","-  5-line decoder straight away (anchor on `ANS-`); do not wait on lib or decompile anything.","-- **Trusting dex `CODEC`/`DAY-NN` strings** (d17-d20 TT): the TT dex drops the tag. Key the decoder on the JSON's fields.","-- **split/indexed order semantics:** two plausible readings exist. Validate against the answer regex instead of guessing.","-- **caesar codec:** shift over raw codepoints, not the alphabet; json-load (escapes `<`/`>`), never regex the raw text.","+- **Single shape != timed shape** (d23): single was v1 `xor`, TT/Mastery v2 computed. A solver tested only on the single","+  (and on old v1 auto cases) emitted nothing in TT and all 7 Mastery sets. Treat a schema bump as a new construct family.","+- **Generalize cut off at CORRECT** (d23): the live worker hand-solved; the generalize workers died before writing the","+  v2 path, so the next day's carried-over solver is still v1-only. Record the method in lib/notes, not in a dead log.","+- **Regex-compose decoys** (d23): the hex table `\"0123456789ABCDEF\"` and `\"ANS-\"` both sit in `Release`; dead mixers make","+  more ANS-shaped values (`ans_compose_scan`). Only the value of `Release.code` reached from ChallengeActivity counts.","+- **Running artifact native code** (d23 `ctypes.CDLL(libarena.so)`): violates the sandbox rule. The export was ~10","+  instructions of arithmetic: read it (`objdump -d`) and port, or unicorn.","+- **Chasing the loopback backend**: ~4 min (d1), ~2.3 min (d6). `127.0.0.1:19090` is the phone's own loopback.","+- **Taking `data` at face value** (d20): an entry path, not a value. Always fullmatch the ANS regex on the final value.","+- **Assuming \"today's codec/schema\" in Mastery** (d15+): sets come from older days, and since d23 even old days are v2.","+- **Reaching for Ghidra on a ~14 KB unstripped `.so`**: `strings`/`nm`/`objdump -d` of the one `Java_*` export first.","+- **New codec, generic solver silent** (d17 `indexed`): write the 5-line decoder straight away, anchored on `ANS-`.","+- **Trusting dex `CODEC`/`DAY-NN` strings or the question's case ref** (d16, d17-d22 TT): key on the JSON and the code.","+- **split/indexed order semantics:** two readings exist; validate against the regex. **caesar:** raw codepoints."," - **Mastery filenames** carry a literal `delivery N: ` prefix. A naive path lookup fails.","-- **Short timed windows** are dominated by start + download + submit; solve is <1 s. No decompiling in-window: the","-  solver runs stdlib + lib.* only, no jadx subprocess.","-- **Prompt wording escalates, the artifact did not** (d8 \"replay the session\", d9 \"exploit a challenge CA\", d12 \"prove","-  server-side impact\", d15 \"split configuration\", d16 \"type or length assumption\", d18 \"strings that reach","-  security-sensitive APIs\", d19 \"reflective dispatch across generated equivalent call graphs\", d20 \"challenge-signed","-  secondary DEX ... module contract\", d21 \"neutralize a clean-room anti-debug state machine while retaining the","-  intended app flow\", d22 \"bypass multiple synthetic root signals without globally patching success\"): judge by what the APK contains (extra entries, `Random`/`Cipher`/`forName`/","-  `DexClassLoader`/`MessageDigest` refs in `strings -a classes.dex`), not by the verb.","-- **Harness, not GM:** a re-start can clobber `single_solve/start.json`; check `hctf status` before re-solving.","-- **Escalation is not monotonic** (d21): after d20's pointer codec the next day was a plain `reverse` again. Keep the","-  whole decoder chain (all codecs + pointer follow + code scanners) in every solver; never drop the old paths.","-- **Manifest flags are not answers** (d21 `debuggable=true`): a flag only matters if code reads it.","-- **Escalation watch:** d20 moved the answer one hop (JSON -> nested dex). Next cheap steps: the payload encrypted /","-  XOR'd / zipped (unwrap by magic known plaintext, key from host dex), several payloads where only the one whose digest","-  matches a pinned hash (\"challenge-signed\") is loaded, >1 `ANS-` in the payload with the host naming the real field/","-  method (`moduleContract`), class shadowing between host and payload, or a stage-2 loader. The resilience arc (d15-d22: native, JNI gate, renaming, string encryption, reflection, dynamic","-  dex, anti-debug, root) still has emulator / hook (Frida, Xposed) / tamper / attestation checks to name; a real gate would put the","-  answer on the CLEAN path of a probe (`clean_device_scan`) and a decoy on the debugged one. If several candidates","-  appear, take the one the code actually returns into `proof=` (`proof_flow_scan`), never the first regex hit.","+- **Timed windows** are start + download + submit; solve must be <1 s pure python (no jadx/javac subprocess in solve.py).","+- **Prompt wording escalated for 22 days while the artifact did not -- then d23 delivered** (d8 \"replay\", d15 \"split\",","+  d19 \"call graphs\", d20 \"signed module\", d21 \"state machine\", d22 \"multiple root signals\", d23 \"real signals vs generated","+  false positives\" = probe results + dead look-alike mixers). Judge by the APK (schema, dex size jump 2.6 -> 5.7 KB,","+  `Release`/`Probe` classes, `native` methods), never by the verb.","+- **Escalation is not monotonic** (d21 back to `reverse` after d20's pointer; d23 single still v1). Keep every decoder.","+- **Escalation watch:** v2 `analysis` is now the timed baseline. Next cheap steps: chain reads Android state (assets","+  JSON `build`, PackageManager signature, Resources, SharedPreferences, `Build.*`) -- stub with the APK's own bytes and a","+  clean retail device; probes that hit hook/emulator/tamper APIs inside the chain (clean answer per signal); flattened","+  or VM-dispatched mixers; Kotlin `object` singletons; JNI in more sets; the `proof` gate demanding a derived input.","\\ No newline at end of file"]}],"originalFile":"# mobile-android — technique log (days 1-22; updated after every day)\n\nHow the lane has looked so far (observations, not guarantees):\n- **Timed variants MUTATE** (organizer, Day 8: \"new, dynamic variations/mutations ... new unseen effects\"): nothing below is a\n  guarantee for Time Trial / Mastery -- solvers derive structure and degrade per field.\n- Every APK so far was the same ~12.7 KB fixture: `AndroidManifest.xml`, `assets/huntress_puzzle.json`, `classes.dex`,\n  `META-INF/FIXTURE-.{SF,RSA}`, `MANIFEST.MF` (6 entries). Extras: d10 `res/xml/network_security_config.xml` +\n  `resources.arsc` (8 entries); d15-d16 `lib/x86_64/libarena.so` (7 entries, ~12.8 KB); d20 `assets/payload.dex` (508 B\n  plain `dex\\n035`, 7 entries, APK 12768 B). d21 = plain 6 entries again (12704 B), but the ONLY manifest so far with\n  `android:debuggable=\"true\"`; d22 plain 6 entries, debuggable false again. One question, `answer` = `ANS-` + 16 uppercase hex.\n- Each day has a new Android IPC/security THEME, written in the manifest `<meta-data android:name=\"huntress.mechanic\">`\n  and in a dex string `DAY-NN:<theme_id>:<mechanic>` (exported Activity, permissive deep link, nested Intent, mutable\n  PendingIntent, allowBackup, exported ContentProvider, JS-interface origin trust, cleartext session, permissive X509\n  trust manager, NSC exception, SharedPreferences credential, client-side SQLite authz, app-controlled Keystore key,\n  predictable nonce d14, `jni_secret` d15, `jni_length` d16, `identifier_obfuscation` d17, `string_decryption` d18,\n  `reflective_dispatch` d19, `dynamic_dex` \"secondary DEX loading\" d20, `anti_debug` \"anti-debug state checks\" d21,\n  `root_detection` \"synthetic root detection\" d22).\n  The theme was mostly flavour: theme stub classes\n  (`WebViewBridge`, `TrustEveryone`, `NativeLibrarySecrets`, `JNIBoundary`, `EncryptedStrings`, `ReflectionMaze`,\n  `LoadedLater`, `DebugMeIfYouCan`, `RootOfTrust`) were never needed, and prompts demanding a live action were still static. d16 had the first REAL gate in\n  code (TT JNI export). **d20 was the first day the answer was NOT in the puzzle JSON**: `data` pointed at a second dex.\n- What varied day to day was the `codec` of `huntress_puzzle.json` (plain, reverse, base64, xor+key, split, hex,\n  caesar+key, then repeats; d15-d16 `native` and d19 `reflection` = theme-named, `data` already the plaintext; d17\n  `indexed` = permutation; d18 back to `xor`; d20 `dynamic` = `data` is a ZIP ENTRY PATH (`assets/payload.dex`) and the\n  answer is a const-string inside that entry; d21 back to `reverse` (3rd time); d22 `base64` (4th: d3/d9/d13)). Keys re-roll per variant. A new codec name is possible any day: check\n  `data` for `ANS-`, then for an entry name in the APK, then decode from the first 4 chars, which must become `ANS-`.\n- **Since d15 Mastery is a MIXED-DAY bundle.** The 5 sets are APKs from earlier days plus one of today's (d15: 01/07/10/\n  14/15; d16: 01/04/11/13/16; d17: 04/08/12/14/17; d18: 03/07/12/13/18; d19: 03/05/11/18/19; d20: d02 reverse, d09\n  base64, d11 xor, d18 xor, d20 dynamic; d21: d03 base64, d10 split, d13 base64, d19 reflection, d21 reverse; d22 = SIX\n  sets: d01 plain, d07 caesar, d12 hex, d13 base64, d17 indexed, d22 base64), all under today's prompt text. Solve each\n  set from its own APK; never assume the set count.\n- In every APK, `.ChallengeActivity` builds a device-loopback URL `http://127.0.0.1:19090/mobile/attempt/<id>/evidence?\n  case_id=..&client_secret=SECRET-..&proof=<answer>`. That backend is NOT reachable (it lives on the phone). The GM\n  accepted the statically recovered value as the \"backend evidence code\" on all 22 days.\n- Pattern d16-d22: the SINGLE variant carries only flavour; the TT build carries the real mechanic as dex strings (d16 JNI\n  gate, d17 `follow b -> a and ignore field c` + `decoy`, d18 `decryptByte` + `STRUCTURAL`, d19 `dispatch` +\n  `STRUCTURAL`, d20 `moduleContract` + `assets/payload.dex:com.huntress.arena.payload.Module` + `STRUCTURAL` -- an\n  `entry:class` pointer, still no `DexClassLoader` API anywhere; d21 `debuggerGate` + `STRUCTURAL`, still no `Debug`/\n  `TracerPid`/clock API; d22 `rootSignals` + `STRUCTURAL`, still no `File`/`Build`/`Runtime.exec`/su API). Read the\n  TT/Mastery APK's dex strings, not just the single's.\n\n## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants -- parse every value listed)\n- **Puzzle codec** -- single + TT always shared the day's codec. `key` (xor byte d4, d11: 81/109/205,29,44,41,232, d16\n  Mastery d04-set 21, d17 d04-set 104, d18: 20/99/233/100, d19 d18-set 44 -- full 0-255 range, never assume printable;\n  caesar shift d7: 10/18/9/3/4/5/15, d14: 9/10/17,4,7,14) and split/offset parameters re-roll per variant: read them from\n  `huntress_puzzle.json` every time. Keyless codecs (`reverse`, `base64`, `native`, `reflection`) differ only in `data` (d21 `reverse`, d22\n  `base64` in single, TT and today's Mastery set).\n  d17 `indexed`: `order[]` was the SAME list in every variant (`order[i] = (3 + 7*i) mod 20`), only `data` changed.\n  d20 `dynamic`: `data` = `assets/payload.dex` in single, TT and the Mastery d20 set (same 508 B payload layout, only the\n  `ANS-` literal changed). Rule: decode by declared codec, regex-check `^ANS-[0-9A-F]{16}$`; if `data` names a zip\n  entry, read that entry and run the whole candidate chain on its bytes; else `decode_any`; unknown name -> known-\n  plaintext `ANS-` trick; any int-list field of len(data) -> try scatter and gather, keep the regex match.\n- **Answer indirection (NEW d20)** -- the JSON value stopped being the answer: it named the entry that holds it. Inside\n  `payload.dex` (class `com.huntress.arena.payload.Module`, strings `ANSWER`, `CONTRACT`, `DAY20-SIGNED-MODULE:<mechanic>`)\n  the only `ANS-` literal was the answer. TT/Mastery host dex also named the class (`<entry>:<dotted class>`) and a method\n  `moduleContract`. Rule: follow the pointer; if the payload ever holds >1 candidate, take the value of the field/method\n  the host names (`ANSWER`, `moduleContract`), not the first regex hit; if the entry is not a valid dex/zip, unwrap it by\n  magic known plaintext (`dex\\n0`, `PK\\x03\\x04`, `\\x7fELF`) before giving up.\n- **Mastery set mix (d15+)** -- sets are fixtures of DIFFERENT days (codec, theme, package `dNN`, extra entries like\n  `res/xml/...`, `lib/x86_64/*.so` or `assets/payload.dex`); the puzzle JSON `day` field and dex `DAY-NN:` tag name the\n  source day. The day picks re-roll per attempt (the pre-start `status` preview lists different MOB-NN than the dealt\n  sets); the last set was always today's, with its own manifest label (cosmetic). d21 picks: d03, d10 (8-entry NSC\n  fixture), d13, d19, d21. d22 picks: d01, d07, d12, d13, d17, d22 (6 sets). d16: the QUESTION's case ref/package did\n  NOT match the APK's own. Rule: per-set, codec-agnostic decoding -- never branch on the day or case ref.\n- **Per-variant identity** -- case ref `MOB-NN-<10 hex>`, package suffix `v<12 hex>`, `client_secret` and the loopback\n  attempt slug change per variant. None of these feed the answer.\n- **Mastery packaging** -- `delivery N: <name>_mastery_0N.apk` per set: pair by sha256. 3 sets (d1-d7, d10-d14), 5\n  (d8, d9, d15-d21) or 6 (d22: `set1..set6.answer`, first time). Loop over the contract's answer_ids, never assume a count.\n- **Dex decoy/hint strings (d17-d22)** -- single dex: `CODEC`, `CONTROL`, `DAY-NN:<theme>:<mechanic>` tag, `describe`; TT\n  and today's Mastery set: NO `DAY-NN` tag and no `describe`, instead the mechanic as strings (sizes single -> TT: d17\n  2588 -> 2672 B, d18 2588 -> 2628, d19 2596 -> 2656, d20 2564 -> 2636, d21 2576 -> 2636 `debuggerGate`, d22 2576 -> 2648 `rootSignals`). Rule: never require `CODEC`/`DAY-NN` to find or\n  decode the puzzle; a TT-only string (`decryptByte`, `dispatch`, `moduleContract`, `debuggerGate`,\n  `rootSignals`) is the cue to the next escalation.\n- **Answer location** -- the puzzle JSON d1-d19 (d15-d16 also in `.so` `.rodata`); d20 a nested asset dex named by the\n  JSON. Fallback chain: `raw_entry_scan`, `dex_strings`, `strings -a lib/*/*.so | grep ANS-`, `extract_answer`.\n- **Manifest flags (d21)** -- `android:debuggable=\"true\"` on all three d21 APKs (single, TT, Mastery d21 set; `aapt\n  dump badging` prints `application-debuggable`), never on older-day sets nor on d22 (theme-local, not a trend). It changed nothing in the decode. Rule:\n  record manifest flags as facts (`manifest_facts`), never let `debuggable`/`allowBackup`/`exported` pick a branch\n  unless dex code reads `ApplicationInfo.flags`/`BuildConfig.DEBUG`; then evaluate the release (non-debug) path.\n- **Native lib shape (d16)** -- single shipped the 13648 B d15-style lib (no `loadLibrary`); TT/Mastery a 14128 B lib with\n  `huntress_arena_length_accepts` + `Java_<pkg>_JNIBoundary_nativeEvidence`. Rule: never key on export names or lib size.\n\n## Recognition cues -> first move\n\n| You see | First move |\n|---|---|\n| `*.apk` artifact, answer_format `ANS- + 16 uppercase hex` | `unzip -l x.apk`, then `unzip -p x.apk assets/huntress_puzzle.json`. triage.md pre-extracts it to `work/extracted/` and prints the JSON |\n| puzzle JSON `{\"codec\":..,\"data\":..}` | decode per codec (table below). Check the result fullmatches `^ANS-[0-9A-F]{16}$` before you submit |\n| `data` is a path (`assets/payload.dex`, codec `dynamic`, d20) | `unzip -p x.apk assets/payload.dex \\| strings -a \\| grep ANS-` (d20: plain const in class `...payload.Module`). Not a dex magic -> known-plaintext unwrap, then recurse |\n| extra `assets/*.dex\\|*.jar\\|*.zip\\|*.bin` (d20) | secondary-code-loading theme: inspect it like `classes.dex`; host strings `<entry>:<class>` + `moduleContract` name the target |\n| int list next to `data` (d17 `indexed`, d5 `split`) | `order[i]` is the OUTPUT slot of `data[i]`: `r[order[i]] = data[i]`. Tell: `A`,`N`,`S`,`-` sit where `order` has 0..3 |\n| Codec name not in the table (d7 `caesar`, d15 `native`, d17 `indexed`, d19 `reflection`, d20 `dynamic`) | `data` already `ANS-`? (d15, d19). An entry name? (d20). Else `data[:4]` vs `ANS-`: constant ord diff = shift, constant XOR = xor key |\n| `lib/<abi>/*.so` (d15-d16 `libarena.so`, ~14 KB, not stripped) | `strings -a lib/*/*.so \\| grep ANS-`, `nm -D --defined-only`; only if no literal, route to binary-re (the `Java_*` export) |\n| Native GATE (d16 `Java_*_nativeEvidence(int)` -> `*_length_accepts`) | the gate only decides whether the `.rodata` literal is returned. Bypass input if ever asked: `objdump -d` the checker (d16: 65536) |\n| No puzzle JSON, or nothing decodes to `ANS-` | `lib.android.extract_answer` (zip scan, dex strings incl. multidex, apktool/jadx), then `strings -a classes*.dex assets/* lib/*/*.so \\| grep ANS-` |\n| Need theme, component, scheme, exported flags | `droidasc getmanifest x.apk`; `aapt dump xmltree x.apk AndroidManifest.xml`; `lib.android.manifest_facts(apk)` |\n| 1-letter classes, hint \"follow b -> a and ignore field c\", `decoy` (d17) | asset first. If the answer leaves it: `jadx --deobf`, follow the chain the hint names; prefer the value that flows into `proof=` |\n| `EncryptedStrings`/`decryptByte` (d18), `ReflectionMaze`/`dispatch` (d19) | asset first. Code-side: `dex_eval_scan` / `reflection_scan`, then `proof_flow_scan` to pick the value that reaches `proof=` |\n| Anti-debug theme: `debuggerGate`, `anti_debug`, manifest `debuggable=true` (d21); later maybe `isDebuggerConnected`, `TracerPid`, `ptrace`, clock deltas | asset first (d21: plain `reverse`, no probe code at all). If code gates the value: `clean_device_scan` (probes answer as a clean retail device), `flattened_cfg_scan` for a `while/switch(state)` loop; take the clean-path value, never run it |\n| Root theme: `rootSignals`, `root_detection`, class `RootOfTrust`, \"multiple root signals\" (d22); later maybe `su` paths, `test-keys`, `magisk`, `Runtime.exec(\"which su\")`, attestation certs | asset first (d22: plain `base64`, no probe code). If code gates the value: `clean_device_scan` per signal (each probe answered as a retail phone), keep the clean-path value; never force the aggregate `isRooted()`/success flag (\"without globally patching success\" = the value may be built from the per-signal results) |\n| Handler logic (URL, extras, constants) | `droidasc findrefs x.apk string <scheme or URL>`, `droidasc getclass x.apk <pkg>.ChallengeActivity`; `jadx -d work/jadx x.apk` |\n| Loopback `127.0.0.1:19090` in the code | do NOT chase it: device-local. The answer is static |\n| Prompt demands a live action (\"replay the session\" d8, \"exploit a CA\" d9, \"challenge-signed\" d20) | still static: `unzip -l` for pcap/HAR/cert/extra dex first. d20's \"signed\" module had no verify code; the v1 `MANIFEST.MF` merely lists its digest |\n| Backup theme with a real `.ab` file (not seen) | 24-byte header + zlib: `dd bs=24 skip=1 \\| zlib-flate -uncompress \\| tar x` |\n| Mastery `delivery N: foo_mastery_0N.apk` | strip the prefix (`lib.common.find_artifact`). Ids `setN.answer`; each set may be another day's fixture |\n\nPuzzle codecs seen (`schema: huntress.mobile.puzzle.v1`):\n- `plain`, `native` (d15-d16, duplicated in the `.so`), `reflection` (d19): `data` is the answer.\n- `dynamic` (d20): `data` = zip entry path; read the entry, `ANS-` literal inside the dex (`puzzle_candidates` yields the\n  path string itself, so the solver's `raw_entry_scan` fallback found it -- follow the pointer explicitly).\n- `reverse` (d2, d8, d21); `base64` (d3, d9, d13, d22); `hex` (d6, d12).\n- `caesar` (d7, d14): `{data, key:int}`, `chr(ord(c) - key)` over EVERY char (digits and `-` too, `KX]7` key 10 -> `ANS-`);\n  a letters-only ROT is wrong. Derive the sign from `data[:4]` vs `ANS-`.\n- `xor` (d4, d11, d18): base64 data, XOR every byte with int `key` (0-255).\n- `split` (d5, d10): `parts[]` + `order[]`, `order[i]` = OUTPUT SLOT of `parts[i]`. Try both readings, keep the `ANS-` one.\n- `indexed` (d17): 20 chars + `order[20]`, `r[order[i]] = data[i]` (`permutation_candidates` tries scatter + gather).\n- `lib.android.decode_payload` / `puzzle_candidates(apk)` / `decode_any` (base32, rot13, `lib.decode.peel`) cover these.\n  Code-side scanners (call yourself; not in `extract_answer`): `renamed_chain_scan`, `proof_flow_scan`, `dex_eval_scan`,\n  `reflection_scan`, `mapping_restore_scan`, `signing_block_scan`, `zip_structure_scan`, `integrity_key_scan`.\n\n## Day by day\n\n**Days 1-6** (same 6-entry fixture, all first try): d1 Exported Trust `plain` (~5.4 min, ~4 min lost probing\n`127.0.0.1:19090`); d2 Deep Link Drift `reverse` (33 s); d3 Intent Injection `base64` (18 s); d4 Pending Intent Relay\n`xor` (77 s); d5 Backup Spill `split` -- `order[i]` = output slot (27 s); d6 Provider Paths `hex` (~3 min, 2.3 min lost on\nthe loopback).\n\n**Days 7-15** (theme stubs never needed; 0 wrong, TT/Mastery 0.8-3.5 s in-window): d7 WebView Bridge new `caesar`; d8\nCleartext Session `reverse`; d9 Trust Everyone `base64`; d10 Network Config Split `split` (8-entry + NSC); d11 Local\nSecrets `xor`; d12 SQLite Assumptions `hex`; d13 Keystore Misuse `base64`; d14 Predictable Crypto `caesar` (json-load the\n`\\\\`/`<` escapes). d15 Native Library Secrets: first `libarena.so` (answer literal in `.rodata`), codec `native` =\nplaintext; first MIXED-DAY Mastery.\n\n**Days 16-19** (asset held the answer; 0 wrong; carried-over solver CORRECT in ~2-25 s): d16 JNI Boundary, `native`; TT\n`.so` added the `nativeEvidence(int)` gate (65536). d17 Name Collapse, NEW `indexed` (race probe silent, duel worker added\nthe decoder -> ~24.5 s); TT hint `follow b -> a and ignore field c`. d18 Encrypted Strings, `xor` (3rd time); TT\n`decryptByte`. d19 Reflection Maze, NEW `reflection` = plaintext; no reflection API in any dex; TT `dispatch`.\n\n**Day 20 — Loaded Later** (`dynamic_dex`): 7-entry APK + `assets/payload.dex` (508 B plain dex). NEW codec `dynamic`:\n`data` = the ENTRY PATH; answer = the only `ANS-` const in `com.huntress.arena.payload.Module`. No ClassLoader/verify\ncode (\"challenge-signed\" was narrative); TT host dex added `moduleContract` + `<entry>:<class>`. Generic `answer()` was\nsilent (pointer string); `raw_entry_scan` found it. CORRECT ~8.4 s; TT 3.06 s, Mastery 5.19 s.\n\n**Day 21 — Debug Me If You Can** (`anti_debug`): plain 6-entry fixture, codec back to `reverse`; the ONLY manifest with\n`android:debuggable=\"true\"`. No `Debug`/`TracerPid`/clock API, no state loop -- \"neutralize a clean-room anti-debug state\nmachine\" was narrative. TT dex added `debuggerGate` + `STRUCTURAL`. Race probe CORRECT ~3.1 s; TT 2.23 s, Mastery 2.10 s.\n\n**Day 22 — Root of Trust** (manifest `huntress.mechanic`=`synthetic root detection`, dex `DAY-22:root_detection:synthetic\nroot detection`, class `RootOfTrust`, deep link `huntress22://root-of-trust/unlock`; prompt \"Model and bypass multiple\nsynthetic root signals without globally patching success.\")\n- Artifact: plain 6-entry fixture (12704 B, dex 2576 B, `debuggable` false), puzzle `{\"codec\":\"base64\",\"data\":\"<b64 of\n  ANS-...>\"}` -- 4th `base64` day. No root probe code in any dex: no `File.exists`, `Build.TAGS`, `Runtime.exec`, su/\n  magisk/test-keys strings. \"Multiple signals\" and \"without globally patching success\" were narrative.\n- TT + today's Mastery set: dex 2648 B, drops the `DAY-22` tag and `describe`, adds `STRUCTURAL`, `rootSignals`,\n  `synthetic root detection`. Same `base64` codec.\n- Mastery: FIRST 6-set bundle (`set1..set6.answer`): d01 plain, d07 caesar, d12 hex, d13 base64, d17 indexed, d22\n  base64. The carried-over solver loops answer_ids, so the extra set cost nothing.\n- Key insight: none needed -- the asset held the answer; the d16-d22 \"TT dex names the mechanic\" pattern held again.\n  Title pun to remember: Android KEY ATTESTATION has an ASN.1 `RootOfTrust` (verifiedBootKey, deviceLocked,\n  verifiedBootState, verifiedBootHash) -- if attestation certs ever ship, that is where to look.\n- Time: race probe CORRECT 9.2 s after start (13:00:11.98Z -> 13:00:21.17Z); the LLM worker only confirmed. TT in-window\n  1.48 s (solve 0.02 s); Mastery 6 sets in-window 1.65 s (solve 0.05 s). `no_clock: true` (d19-d22). All first try, 0\n  wrong. GM spelling unchanged: `answer` / `setN.answer`, `exact`.\n\n## GM answer conventions learned\n- One field, `answer`. Single solve and TT use id `answer`; Mastery uses `setN.answer` (3, 5 or 6 sets), one APK per set.\n- Format is `ANS-` + exactly 16 UPPERCASE hex, normalization `exact`. Uppercase the hex after decoding, no whitespace.\n- No mobile answer has ever been rejected (zero wrong submissions on days 1-22). The GM accepts the statically recovered\n  value as the \"backend evidence code\" even though the prompt says \"Submit only the exact backend answer code\".\n- Mastery feedback is per set: `{\"result\":\"accepted\",\"remaining\":N}` after each set, then `CORRECT` on the last. An\n  empty submit after the deadline returns `expired`.\n- Prompt boilerplate: \"For case MOB-NN-<10 hex> in package com.huntress.mobile.dNN.v<12 hex>\". In Mastery the text is\n  today's and the case ref may not match the APK (d16). Neither was ever needed for the answer.\n\n## Pitfalls that cost time\n- **Chasing the loopback backend** was the only recurring time sink: ~4 min (d1), ~30 s (d4), ~2.3 min (d6).\n  `127.0.0.1:19090` is the phone's own loopback. If a static value matches the answer_format, submit it.\n- **Taking `data` at face value** (d20): `data` was an entry path, not a value. Never submit or \"decode\" a string that\n  names a zip entry; open the entry. Always fullmatch the ANS regex on the final value.\n- **Assuming \"today's codec\" in Mastery** (d15+): sets come from older days with different codecs and extra entries.\n- **Reaching for Ghidra on a native-lib theme** (d15-d16): the `.so` is ~14 KB, unstripped, the answer a literal. Use\n  `strings`/`nm`, then `objdump -d` of the one `Java_*` export. Same for d20's payload: `strings` before `jadx`.\n- **Trusting the question's case ref in Mastery** (d16): it can name a different day/case than the APK it points at.\n- **New codec, generic solver silent** (d17 `indexed`, ~20 s lost): when the JSON has an unknown codec, write the\n  5-line decoder straight away (anchor on `ANS-`); do not wait on lib or decompile anything.\n- **Trusting dex `CODEC`/`DAY-NN` strings** (d17-d20 TT): the TT dex drops the tag. Key the decoder on the JSON's fields.\n- **split/indexed order semantics:** two plausible readings exist. Validate against the answer regex instead of guessing.\n- **caesar codec:** shift over raw codepoints, not the alphabet; json-load (escapes `<`/`>`), never regex the raw text.\n- **Mastery filenames** carry a literal `delivery N: ` prefix. A naive path lookup fails.\n- **Short timed windows** are dominated by start + download + submit; solve is <1 s. No decompiling in-window: the\n  solver runs stdlib + lib.* only, no jadx subprocess.\n- **Prompt wording escalates, the artifact did not** (d8 \"replay the session\", d9 \"exploit a challenge CA\", d12 \"prove\n  server-side impact\", d15 \"split configuration\", d16 \"type or length assumption\", d18 \"strings that reach\n  security-sensitive APIs\", d19 \"reflective dispatch across generated equivalent call graphs\", d20 \"challenge-signed\n  secondary DEX ... module contract\", d21 \"neutralize a clean-room anti-debug state machine while retaining the\n  intended app flow\", d22 \"bypass multiple synthetic root signals without globally patching success\"): judge by what the APK contains (extra entries, `Random`/`Cipher`/`forName`/\n  `DexClassLoader`/`MessageDigest` refs in `strings -a classes.dex`), not by the verb.\n- **Harness, not GM:** a re-start can clobber `single_solve/start.json`; check `hctf status` before re-solving.\n- **Escalation is not monotonic** (d21): after d20's pointer codec the next day was a plain `reverse` again. Keep the\n  whole decoder chain (all codecs + pointer follow + code scanners) in every solver; never drop the old paths.\n- **Manifest flags are not answers** (d21 `debuggable=true`): a flag only matters if code reads it.\n- **Escalation watch:** d20 moved the answer one hop (JSON -> nested dex). Next cheap steps: the payload encrypted /\n  XOR'd / zipped (unwrap by magic known plaintext, key from host dex), several payloads where only the one whose digest\n  matches a pinned hash (\"challenge-signed\") is loaded, >1 `ANS-` in the payload with the host naming the real field/\n  method (`moduleContract`), class shadowing between host and payload, or a stage-2 loader. The resilience arc (d15-d22: native, JNI gate, renaming, string encryption, reflection, dynamic\n  dex, anti-debug, root) still has emulator / hook (Frida, Xposed) / tamper / attestation checks to name; a real gate would put the\n  answer on the CLEAN path of a probe (`clean_device_scan`) and a decoy on the debugged one. If several candidates\n  appear, take the one the code actually returns into `proof=` (`proof_flow_scan`), never the first regex hit.\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01SD5RftAGy4oxSHgWdWcHnm","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
