{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgKFptt2PSAKvw2Z3h4T5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018J5qCJTzf52jD1zq79r8Ng","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; cat > $TMPDIR/gaps.py <<'PYEOF'\nimport json, re\np='reference/coverage/mobile-android.md'\nt=open(p).read()\na=t.index(\"## Readiness gaps\")\nold=json.loads(re.search(r\"```json\\n(.*?)```\",t[a:],re.S).group(1))\nkeep_ids=[\"play-integrity-verdict-select\",\"worker-cue-inline\",\"pyxamstore\",\"apkid\",\"bundletool\",\"ios-ipa-readiness\",\"il2cppdumper\",\"blutter\",\"abe\",\"frida-tools\",\"standalone-baksmali\"]\nkeep={g[\"id\"]:g for g in old if g[\"id\"] in keep_ids}\nassert len(keep)==len(keep_ids)\nnew=[\n {\"id\":\"analysis-release-code-eval\",\"concept\":\"puzzle v2 `analysis`: evaluate the answer-producing method (`Release.code(Context)`) in pure python (rows 69, 96, 97, 98)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D23 TT + all 7 Mastery sets shipped `{\\\"schema\\\":\\\"huntress.mobile.puzzle.v2\\\",\\\"codec\\\":\\\"analysis\\\",\\\"build\\\":..}` with no data; the carried-over solver was silent and `bytecode_vm_scan`/_DxVM resolved only 2 of 8 APKs. Build `analysis_scan(apk)` and call it from extract_answer/puzzle_candidates when the puzzle has no `data` or codec == analysis: (1) locate the entry: the method whose String result ChallengeActivity appends before `&proof=` (fallback: any static `(Landroid/content/Context;)Ljava/lang/String;` on a class named Release, then any static method returning a String that starts with const `ANS-`); (2) run it in the lib Dalvik evaluator with a stub Context object (sput-object to a static must work), executing <clinit> of every touched class first (K consts may be computed, not const-wide), full long ALU (add/sub/mul/xor/or/and/shl/shr/ushr-long incl. /2addr and lit forms, int<->long conversions, cmp-long), new-array/aget-wide/aput-wide/fill-array-data, StringBuilder.append(String|char), String.charAt, Long.toHexString, loops of up to ~4096*N iterations (Probe.s1/s2/s3 inverse searches) with a step budget >= 5M and wall clock <0.8 s per APK; (3) also evaluate `Release.proof` and report consistency (proof == Long.toHexString(token)). Return only the value produced by the entry, never regex-composed candidates. Regression fixtures: the 8 v2 APKs under challenges/day23/mobile-hook-line-and-signal (TT + mastery attempt 1d39aa76, set5 needs the native bridge).\"},\n {\"id\":\"dex-eval-native-bridge\",\"concept\":\"Dalvik evaluator calls a `native` method mid-chain by emulating its `Java_*` export (rows 37, 96)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D23 Mastery d15 set: `NativeLibrarySecrets.nativeShare(long)` (static native, `System.loadLibrary(\\\"arena\\\")` in <clinit>) sits inside Release.token(); `lib/x86_64/libarena.so` (13512 B) exports `Java_<pkg>_NativeLibrarySecrets_nativeShare` = ~10 insns of movabs/add/xor/imul/rol on rdx. The LLM worker used ctypes.CDLL on the host (sandbox violation). In the evaluator: when invoke-static/virtual hits a method with ACC_NATIVE, mangle the JNI name (incl. overloaded `__<sig>` form and `_1`/`_0xxxx` escapes), find the export in lib/<abi>/*.so (x86_64 first, then arm64-v8a/armeabi-v7a/x86), and run it under unicorn (reuse native-so-emulate-export): JNIEnv* -> a fake function table whose slots return 0/trap, jclass/jobject = dummy handles, long/int args per SysV (rdx, rcx, r8...) or AAPCS64 (x2, x3...), return rax/x0 masked to the declared type; jstring returns via a NewStringUTF stub that records the C string. Budget 200k insns. Also support RegisterNatives tables (registernatives-table built). Never dlopen the artifact.\"},\n {\"id\":\"analysis-android-api-stubs\",\"concept\":\"v2 chain reads Android state through the Context it is handed: answer from the APK's own bytes + a clean retail device (row 99)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D23 `Release.code(Context)` stores ctx in a static but never reads it -- a loaded gun for the next days (emulator/tamper/attestation themes). Give the evaluator Context stubs that answer from the APK itself: getAssets().open(name) -> zip entry bytes (InputStream read/readAllBytes/available), org.json JSONObject(String).getString/getInt/getLong/optString (so `build`/`day` fields can seed the chain), getResources().getString(id)/getIdentifier via resources.arsc (resource-id-const-resolve built), getPackageName() -> manifest package, getPackageManager().getPackageInfo(pkg, GET_SIGNATURES|GET_SIGNING_CERTIFICATES) -> real cert bytes (signing_certs), versionCode/versionName/firstInstallTime constants, getApplicationInfo().flags from the manifest (debuggable bit), getSharedPreferences -> empty with defaults returned, Build.FINGERPRINT/MODEL/MANUFACTURER/BRAND/HARDWARE/TAGS/TYPE -> a retail Pixel (release-keys, user), Settings.Secure ANDROID_ID -> fixed 16 hex, System.getProperty -> JVM-like defaults, SystemClock/nanoTime monotonic small deltas. Plug in the existing clean_device_scan probe tables (emulator/hook/root/installer) so a probe inside the chain gets the clean answer. Log every stub hit for the worker.\"},\n {\"id\":\"dex-eval-pure-static-memo\",\"concept\":\"keep a pure-python Dalvik evaluation of a v2 chain under the timed budget for 7+ sets (rows 96, 97)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Mastery grew to 7 sets (D23) and each solve must stay <1 s total. v2 chains call Probe.s1/s2/s3 (up to 4096 iterations of ~10 ops) 3-6 times per set plus table walks. Add: memoisation of static methods whose bodies touch no static fields/arrays/invokes outside the pure set (key = method + args); a recognizer that turns `i=0; while(f(i)!=t){i++; if(i>=N) return -1}` into a direct python loop over a compiled lambda of f; precompiled per-method python closures (translate the straight-line long-ALU basic blocks once, then run); per-set fork already exists in solverrt. Target: all 8 day23 v2 APKs < 0.3 s each on the Homebase VM.\"},\n {\"id\":\"entry-anchored-candidate-veto\",\"concept\":\"reject ANS-shaped candidates that the entry method does not produce: hex-table and dead-mixer decoys (row 98)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D23 v2 dex holds `ANS-` and `0123456789ABCDEF` consts in Release plus unreferenced look-alike mixers (`sealTrampolinec7`, `sealHook30`, `K*` longs); `ans_compose_scan` returned several ANS-shaped DECOYS and a naive compose gives `ANS-0123456789ABCDEF` (also the harness placeholder). In extract_answer's ranking: when an entry-evaluated value exists (analysis_scan/proof_flow_scan), drop every other code-side candidate; never emit a candidate equal to the hex alphabet; demote candidates from methods unreachable from ChallengeActivity/MainActivity (entry-reachable-callgraph-rank built) and from fns whose only callers are themselves dead. Unit test on the day23 TT APK: only ANS-E4F679E90A7D1CAE-shaped output from Release.code survives.\"},\n {\"id\":\"dex-eval-long-intrinsics\",\"concept\":\"java.lang / kotlin intrinsics a mixer chain may call (row 96)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D23 mixers inline rotates as shl/ushr pairs; the next generator may call the library: Long.rotateLeft/rotateRight/reverse/reverseBytes/bitCount/numberOfLeadingZeros/numberOfTrailingZeros/highestOneBit/signum, Long.divideUnsigned/remainderUnsigned/compareUnsigned/toUnsignedString/parseUnsignedLong/parseLong(s,16)/toString(v,36), Integer.* equivalents, Math.floorMod/floorDiv/abs/multiplyHigh/multiplyExact (raise on overflow), Math.multiplyHigh/unsignedMultiplyHigh, String.format(\\\"%016X\\\"|\\\"%016x\\\"|\\\"%08X\\\", ..) and Locale variants, Long.hashCode, String.hashCode, Arrays.hashCode, CRC32/Adler32 update/getValue, MessageDigest SHA-256/MD5 over byte[] (+ BigInteger(1,d).toString(16)), kotlin ULong ops (`ULong.constructor-impl`, `UnsignedKt.ulongRemainder`, `Long.rotateLeft` in kotlin.Bits). Implement in the evaluator's intrinsic table with exact Java semantics (two's complement wrap, sign extension).\"},\n {\"id\":\"kotlin-object-chain-eval\",\"concept\":\"v2 chain written in Kotlin: `object` singletons, companion objects, @JvmStatic, top-level `*Kt` classes, inline classes (row 96)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"The D23 chain is plain static Java. A Kotlin build would compile Mix.f1 to `Mix.INSTANCE.f1(j)` (sget-object INSTANCE + invoke-virtual/final), companion `Release.Companion.code(ctx)`, top-level fns in `ReleaseKt`, `Intrinsics.checkNotNullParameter` calls, `ULong` boxing (`ULong.box-impl`), lambdas (`$$ExternalSyntheticLambda0`, invoke-custom), `when` -> sparse-switch. Make the evaluator: run <clinit> to build INSTANCE/Companion, dispatch invoke-virtual on singleton receivers by class, treat kotlin.jvm.internal.Intrinsics.* as no-ops, unbox inline classes, follow synthetic accessor `access$`. Test with a tiny hand-built dex (dexlib-free: reuse the lib's dex writer fixture if present, else skip with a TODO).\"},\n {\"id\":\"instrumentation-false-positive-env\",\"concept\":\"hook/instrumentation detection where generated benign signals must evaluate as false positives: realistic clean process introspection (rows 48, 91)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D23 prompt 'Separate real instrumentation signals from generated false positives' shipped only arithmetic, but a real version scores signals: /proc/self/maps lines (libart, libc, libandroid_runtime, app base.apk, `[anon:dalvik-...]`, a benign `libfrida_like_name` or `gadget` substring in an unrelated path), Thread.getAllStackTraces / Throwable stack frames (com.android.internal.os.ZygoteInit, RuntimeInit, android.app.ActivityThread -- no de.robv.android.xposed / com.saurik.substrate), /proc/self/task/*/comm names (main, RenderThread, FinalizerDaemon, HeapTaskDaemon -- no gum-js-loop/gmain/pool-frida), open ports (/proc/net/tcp without 27042/27043), Modifier.isNative on the app's own methods (only declared natives), ClassLoader.loadClass('de.robv.android.xposed.XposedBridge') -> ClassNotFoundException, Debug.isDebuggerConnected false, installed packages without frida/xposed/lsposed managers. Extend hook-framework-introspection-stubs (built) so each probe returns this realistic clean text (with deliberate near-miss substrings) and the app's own filter logic decides; report per-signal verdicts so the worker can see which ones were 'false positives'.\"},\n {\"id\":\"analysis-chain-obfuscation-hardening\",\"concept\":\"v2 mixers behind flattening / opaque predicates / string-switch dispatch / reflection (rows 72, 77, 79, 81, 96)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"The resilience arc (D17 renaming, D18 strings, D19 reflection, D21 state machine) can now be applied to the v2 chain itself: token() split into a `while(true){switch(state)}` dispatcher, mixers invoked via Class.forName/getDeclaredMethod with xor'd names, opaque predicates guarding a decoy mixer, a tiny bytecode VM running the mix. Wire flattened-cfg-switch-eval, reflection-name-resolve, opaque-predicate-dead-branch and tiny-bytecode-vm-interpret (all built) into analysis_scan's evaluator (reflection: resolve Method objects to dex methods and invoke them; Method.invoke boxing/unboxing of Long), with the same <0.8 s budget. Synthetic test: the D23 TT chain rewritten with each transform.\"},\n]\ngaps=[keep[\"worker-cue-inline\"]]\ngaps+=new[:4]\ngaps+=[keep[\"play-integrity-verdict-select\"]]\ngaps+=new[4:]\ngaps+=[keep[i] for i in [\"pyxamstore\",\"apkid\",\"bundletool\",\"ios-ipa-readiness\",\"il2cppdumper\",\"blutter\",\"abe\",\"frida-tools\",\"standalone-baksmali\"]]\n# insert a note gap\ngaps.insert(1,{\"id\":\"generalize-before-stop\",\"concept\":\"carry the hand-solved method into solve.py when a live worker reaches CORRECT first\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"note\",\"detail\":\"D23: TT/Mastery were hand-solved (jadx + javac) while the generalize workers were cut off at CORRECT, so solve.py kept no v2 path and tomorrow's Mastery (which mixes old days, now regenerated as v2) would be silent again. Harness note: when a timed mode is CORRECT via a live worker, let one generalize worker finish (offline, no clock) and require a passing `hctf solver-test` on the variant-* cases with expected.json filled from confirmed.json (D23 variant cases have expected {}).\"})\nbuilt_prev=\"\"\"aab-proto-manifest-parse, ans-prefix-numeric-compose, anti-debug-state-machine-clean-path, apk-signing-block-payload,\nasset-cipher-dex-loader, asset-db-prefs-backup, attestation-jws-claims, binder-ontransact-code-map,\"\"\"\nassert built_prev in t\nt2=t[:a]\nsec=\"\"\"## Readiness gaps\n\nPriority 1 = plausible within ~3 days. \"prebuild\" = pure-python extractor in `lib/android.py` style that races in\n`solve.py`. \"tool\" = install. \"note\" = doc/prompt change. Already built (prebuild-state ok, dropped from the list):\naab-proto-manifest-parse, ans-prefix-numeric-compose, anti-debug-state-machine-clean-path, apk-signing-block-payload,\nasset-cipher-dex-loader, asset-db-prefs-backup, attestation-jws-claims, binder-ontransact-code-map,\nbiometric-auth-callback-eval, broadcast-receiver-action-map, cdex-vdex-string-pool, cert-and-signing-facts,\ncert-pin-and-nsc-facts, classloader-shadow-resolve, clean-device-env-stubs, custom-alphabet-decode,\ndalvik-mini-interpreter, dart-snapshot-string-pool, decode-any-chain-peel, decrypt-call-site-args-eval,\ndex-bytecode-integrity-gate, dex-gated-branch-consts, dex-native-call-args, dex-native-split-assembly,\ndex-slack-and-header-anomaly, dex-string-decrypt-arrays, dispatch-key-resolve, emulator-telephony-sensor-stubs,\nentry-reachable-callgraph-rank, enum-switchmap-state-resolve, exception-driven-control-flow, flattened-cfg-switch-eval,\nhermes-hbc-string-table, hook-framework-introspection-stubs, identifier-collision-resolve, identity-derived-key,\nil2cpp-metadata-literals, installer-source-and-tamper-probe-stubs, integrity-derived-key, java-serialized-object-parse,\njni-export-return-trace, jni-gate-bypass-input, jni-reflection-callback, jwt-token-decode-verify,\nkey-attestation-rootoftrust-parse, known-string-obfuscator-signatures, kotlin-metadata-names-and-coroutines,\nmessagedigest-derived-answer, module-contract-member-eval, multi-abi-arm-native, multi-stage-loader-recurse,\nnative-gated-branch-read, native-init-array-decrypt, native-inline-syscall-stubs, native-libc-probe-stubs-emulate,\nnative-payload-system-load, native-so-emulate-export, native-stack-string, native-system-property-and-mounts-stubs,\nnested-container-recurse, opaque-predicate-dead-branch, payload-digest-pinned-select,\npayload-magic-known-plaintext-unwrap, permutation-transposition-family, probe-arg-resolve-before-stub,\nprocess-exec-shell-probe-stubs, proguard-mapping-restore, proof-flow-candidate-ranking, protobuf-asset-wire-decode,\nproxy-methodhandle-invokecustom, puzzle-entry-pointer-follow, puzzle-indexed-and-perm-fields, r8-renamed-chain-follow,\nreflection-name-resolve, registernatives-table, resource-id-const-resolve, rolling-xor-keystream-family,\nroot-signal-vector-key, sqlcipher-asset-decrypt, static-key-cipher-decode, timing-and-debug-flag-probe-stubs,\ntiny-bytecode-vm-interpret, utf16-string-pool-scan, v1-manifest-digest-verify, webview-asset-js-scan,\nwhitebox-table-cipher-eval, xamarin-xalz-blob-unpack, zip-structure-anomaly-scan.\nForecast after D23: the MASVS-RESILIENCE arc continues one control per day (D21 anti-debug, D22 root, D23 hook/\ninstrumentation); still unnamed: emulator detection, tamper/repackaging/installer/signature, attestation (Play Integrity,\nkey attestation), then obfuscation capstones (flattening, VM, white-box). The big change is structural: since D23 the\ntimed builds (TT + every Mastery set, old days included) COMPUTE the answer in dex (`Release.code`), so each new theme\nwill most likely arrive as a gate fn / probe set inside that chain, and soon as real Android API reads through the\nContext it already receives. Priority 1 = a fast, sandbox-safe v2 evaluator (incl. JNI bridge and Context stubs).\n\n```json\n\"\"\"+json.dumps(gaps,indent=None,ensure_ascii=False).replace('}, {\"id\"','},\\n  {\"id\"').replace('[{\"id\"','[\\n  {\"id\"').replace('}]','}\\n]')+\"\"\"\n```\n\"\"\"\nopen(p,'w').write(t2+sec)\nPYEOF\npython3 $TMPDIR/gaps.py && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json,re\nt=open('reference/coverage/mobile-android.md').read()\ng=json.loads(re.search(r\"```json\\n(.*?)```\",t,re.S).group(1))\ns=json.load(open('.run/prebuild-state.json'))\npend=[x['id'] for x in g if x['action']=='prebuild' and not (s.get('mobile-android:'+x['id'],{}).get('ok') or s.get('mobile-android:'+x['id'],{}).get('attempts',0)>=2)]\nprint(len(g), 'pending prebuild', len(pend), pend)\nassert all(set(x)=={'id','concept','priority','action','detail'} for x in g)\nprint(len(set(x['id'] for x in g))==len(g))\nEOF\ntail -c 600 reference/coverage/mobile-android.md; wc -l reference/coverage/mobile-android.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2893,"cache_read_input_tokens":128132,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2893},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c40b34bd-42fb-42e5-b584-d0c2bd140aef","uuid":"e474689a-e399-4098-8d46-1c30a8c8ac6a","timestamp":"2026-10-23T13:36:20.742Z","request_id":"req_011CgKFptZvZ2zwdWo55aYcc","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_018J5qCJTzf52jD1zq79r8Ng":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; cat > $TMPDIR/gaps.py <<'PYEOF'\nimport json, re\np='reference/coverage/mobile-android.md'\nt=open(p).read()\na=t.index(\"## Readiness gaps\")\nold=json.loads(re.search(r\"```json\\n(.*?)```\",t[a:],re.S).group(1))\nkeep_ids=[\"play-integrity-verdict-select\",\"worker-cue-inline\",\"pyxamstore\",\"apkid\",\"bundletool\",\"ios-ipa-readiness\",\"il2cppdumper\",\"blutter\",\"abe\",\"frida-tools\",\"standalone-baksmali\"]\nkeep={g[\"id\"]:g for g in old if g[\"id\"] in keep_ids}\nassert len(keep)==len(keep_ids)\nnew=[\n {\"id\":\"analysis-release-code-eval\",\"concept\":\"puzzle v2 `analysis`: evaluate the answer-producing method (`Release.code(Context)`) in pure python (rows 69, 96, 97, 98)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D23 TT + all 7 Mastery sets shipped `{\\\"schema\\\":\\\"huntress.mobile.puzzle.v2\\\",\\\"codec\\\":\\\"analysis\\\",\\\"build\\\":..}` with no data; the carried-over solver was silent and `bytecode_vm_scan`/_DxVM resolved only 2 of 8 APKs. Build `analysis_scan(apk)` and call it from extract_answer/puzzle_candidates when the puzzle has no `data` or codec == analysis: (1) locate the entry: the method whose String result ChallengeActivity appends before `&proof=` (fallback: any static `(Landroid/content/Context;)Ljava/lang/String;` on a class named Release, then any static method returning a String that starts with const `ANS-`); (2) run it in the lib Dalvik evaluator with a stub Context object (sput-object to a static must work), executing <clinit> of every touched class first (K consts may be computed, not const-wide), full long ALU (add/sub/mul/xor/or/and/shl/shr/ushr-long incl. /2addr and lit forms, int<->long conversions, cmp-long), new-array/aget-wide/aput-wide/fill-array-data, StringBuilder.append(String|char), String.charAt, Long.toHexString, loops of up to ~4096*N iterations (Probe.s1/s2/s3 inverse searches) with a step budget >= 5M and wall clock <0.8 s per APK; (3) also evaluate `Release.proof` and report consistency (proof == Long.toHexString(token)). Return only the value produced by the entry, never regex-composed candidates. Regression fixtures: the 8 v2 APKs under challenges/day23/mobile-hook-line-and-signal (TT + mastery attempt 1d39aa76, set5 needs the native bridge).\"},\n {\"id\":\"dex-eval-native-bridge\",\"concept\":\"Dalvik evaluator calls a `native` method mid-chain by emulating its `Java_*` export (rows 37, 96)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D23 Mastery d15 set: `NativeLibrarySecrets.nativeShare(long)` (static native, `System.loadLibrary(\\\"arena\\\")` in <clinit>) sits inside Release.token(); `lib/x86_64/libarena.so` (13512 B) exports `Java_<pkg>_NativeLibrarySecrets_nativeShare` = ~10 insns of movabs/add/xor/imul/rol on rdx. The LLM worker used ctypes.CDLL on the host (sandbox violation). In the evaluator: when invoke-static/virtual hits a method with ACC_NATIVE, mangle the JNI name (incl. overloaded `__<sig>` form and `_1`/`_0xxxx` escapes), find the export in lib/<abi>/*.so (x86_64 first, then arm64-v8a/armeabi-v7a/x86), and run it under unicorn (reuse native-so-emulate-export): JNIEnv* -> a fake function table whose slots return 0/trap, jclass/jobject = dummy handles, long/int args per SysV (rdx, rcx, r8...) or AAPCS64 (x2, x3...), return rax/x0 masked to the declared type; jstring returns via a NewStringUTF stub that records the C string. Budget 200k insns. Also support RegisterNatives tables (registernatives-table built). Never dlopen the artifact.\"},\n {\"id\":\"analysis-android-api-stubs\",\"concept\":\"v2 chain reads Android state through the Context it is handed: answer from the APK's own bytes + a clean retail device (row 99)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D23 `Release.code(Context)` stores ctx in a static but never reads it -- a loaded gun for the next days (emulator/tamper/attestation themes). Give the evaluator Context stubs that answer from the APK itself: getAssets().open(name) -> zip entry bytes (InputStream read/readAllBytes/available), org.json JSONObject(String).getString/getInt/getLong/optString (so `build`/`day` fields can seed the chain), getResources().getString(id)/getIdentifier via resources.arsc (resource-id-const-resolve built), getPackageName() -> manifest package, getPackageManager().getPackageInfo(pkg, GET_SIGNATURES|GET_SIGNING_CERTIFICATES) -> real cert bytes (signing_certs), versionCode/versionName/firstInstallTime constants, getApplicationInfo().flags from the manifest (debuggable bit), getSharedPreferences -> empty with defaults returned, Build.FINGERPRINT/MODEL/MANUFACTURER/BRAND/HARDWARE/TAGS/TYPE -> a retail Pixel (release-keys, user), Settings.Secure ANDROID_ID -> fixed 16 hex, System.getProperty -> JVM-like defaults, SystemClock/nanoTime monotonic small deltas. Plug in the existing clean_device_scan probe tables (emulator/hook/root/installer) so a probe inside the chain gets the clean answer. Log every stub hit for the worker.\"},\n {\"id\":\"dex-eval-pure-static-memo\",\"concept\":\"keep a pure-python Dalvik evaluation of a v2 chain under the timed budget for 7+ sets (rows 96, 97)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Mastery grew to 7 sets (D23) and each solve must stay <1 s total. v2 chains call Probe.s1/s2/s3 (up to 4096 iterations of ~10 ops) 3-6 times per set plus table walks. Add: memoisation of static methods whose bodies touch no static fields/arrays/invokes outside the pure set (key = method + args); a recognizer that turns `i=0; while(f(i)!=t){i++; if(i>=N) return -1}` into a direct python loop over a compiled lambda of f; precompiled per-method python closures (translate the straight-line long-ALU basic blocks once, then run); per-set fork already exists in solverrt. Target: all 8 day23 v2 APKs < 0.3 s each on the Homebase VM.\"},\n {\"id\":\"entry-anchored-candidate-veto\",\"concept\":\"reject ANS-shaped candidates that the entry method does not produce: hex-table and dead-mixer decoys (row 98)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D23 v2 dex holds `ANS-` and `0123456789ABCDEF` consts in Release plus unreferenced look-alike mixers (`sealTrampolinec7`, `sealHook30`, `K*` longs); `ans_compose_scan` returned several ANS-shaped DECOYS and a naive compose gives `ANS-0123456789ABCDEF` (also the harness placeholder). In extract_answer's ranking: when an entry-evaluated value exists (analysis_scan/proof_flow_scan), drop every other code-side candidate; never emit a candidate equal to the hex alphabet; demote candidates from methods unreachable from ChallengeActivity/MainActivity (entry-reachable-callgraph-rank built) and from fns whose only callers are themselves dead. Unit test on the day23 TT APK: only ANS-E4F679E90A7D1CAE-shaped output from Release.code survives.\"},\n {\"id\":\"dex-eval-long-intrinsics\",\"concept\":\"java.lang / kotlin intrinsics a mixer chain may call (row 96)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D23 mixers inline rotates as shl/ushr pairs; the next generator may call the library: Long.rotateLeft/rotateRight/reverse/reverseBytes/bitCount/numberOfLeadingZeros/numberOfTrailingZeros/highestOneBit/signum, Long.divideUnsigned/remainderUnsigned/compareUnsigned/toUnsignedString/parseUnsignedLong/parseLong(s,16)/toString(v,36), Integer.* equivalents, Math.floorMod/floorDiv/abs/multiplyHigh/multiplyExact (raise on overflow), Math.multiplyHigh/unsignedMultiplyHigh, String.format(\\\"%016X\\\"|\\\"%016x\\\"|\\\"%08X\\\", ..) and Locale variants, Long.hashCode, String.hashCode, Arrays.hashCode, CRC32/Adler32 update/getValue, MessageDigest SHA-256/MD5 over byte[] (+ BigInteger(1,d).toString(16)), kotlin ULong ops (`ULong.constructor-impl`, `UnsignedKt.ulongRemainder`, `Long.rotateLeft` in kotlin.Bits). Implement in the evaluator's intrinsic table with exact Java semantics (two's complement wrap, sign extension).\"},\n {\"id\":\"kotlin-object-chain-eval\",\"concept\":\"v2 chain written in Kotlin: `object` singletons, companion objects, @JvmStatic, top-level `*Kt` classes, inline classes (row 96)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"The D23 chain is plain static Java. A Kotlin build would compile Mix.f1 to `Mix.INSTANCE.f1(j)` (sget-object INSTANCE + invoke-virtual/final), companion `Release.Companion.code(ctx)`, top-level fns in `ReleaseKt`, `Intrinsics.checkNotNullParameter` calls, `ULong` boxing (`ULong.box-impl`), lambdas (`$$ExternalSyntheticLambda0`, invoke-custom), `when` -> sparse-switch. Make the evaluator: run <clinit> to build INSTANCE/Companion, dispatch invoke-virtual on singleton receivers by class, treat kotlin.jvm.internal.Intrinsics.* as no-ops, unbox inline classes, follow synthetic accessor `access$`. Test with a tiny hand-built dex (dexlib-free: reuse the lib's dex writer fixture if present, else skip with a TODO).\"},\n {\"id\":\"instrumentation-false-positive-env\",\"concept\":\"hook/instrumentation detection where generated benign signals must evaluate as false positives: realistic clean process introspection (rows 48, 91)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D23 prompt 'Separate real instrumentation signals from generated false positives' shipped only arithmetic, but a real version scores signals: /proc/self/maps lines (libart, libc, libandroid_runtime, app base.apk, `[anon:dalvik-...]`, a benign `libfrida_like_name` or `gadget` substring in an unrelated path), Thread.getAllStackTraces / Throwable stack frames (com.android.internal.os.ZygoteInit, RuntimeInit, android.app.ActivityThread -- no de.robv.android.xposed / com.saurik.substrate), /proc/self/task/*/comm names (main, RenderThread, FinalizerDaemon, HeapTaskDaemon -- no gum-js-loop/gmain/pool-frida), open ports (/proc/net/tcp without 27042/27043), Modifier.isNative on the app's own methods (only declared natives), ClassLoader.loadClass('de.robv.android.xposed.XposedBridge') -> ClassNotFoundException, Debug.isDebuggerConnected false, installed packages without frida/xposed/lsposed managers. Extend hook-framework-introspection-stubs (built) so each probe returns this realistic clean text (with deliberate near-miss substrings) and the app's own filter logic decides; report per-signal verdicts so the worker can see which ones were 'false positives'.\"},\n {\"id\":\"analysis-chain-obfuscation-hardening\",\"concept\":\"v2 mixers behind flattening / opaque predicates / string-switch dispatch / reflection (rows 72, 77, 79, 81, 96)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"The resilience arc (D17 renaming, D18 strings, D19 reflection, D21 state machine) can now be applied to the v2 chain itself: token() split into a `while(true){switch(state)}` dispatcher, mixers invoked via Class.forName/getDeclaredMethod with xor'd names, opaque predicates guarding a decoy mixer, a tiny bytecode VM running the mix. Wire flattened-cfg-switch-eval, reflection-name-resolve, opaque-predicate-dead-branch and tiny-bytecode-vm-interpret (all built) into analysis_scan's evaluator (reflection: resolve Method objects to dex methods and invoke them; Method.invoke boxing/unboxing of Long), with the same <0.8 s budget. Synthetic test: the D23 TT chain rewritten with each transform.\"},\n]\ngaps=[keep[\"worker-cue-inline\"]]\ngaps+=new[:4]\ngaps+=[keep[\"play-integrity-verdict-select\"]]\ngaps+=new[4:]\ngaps+=[keep[i] for i in [\"pyxamstore\",\"apkid\",\"bundletool\",\"ios-ipa-readiness\",\"il2cppdumper\",\"blutter\",\"abe\",\"frida-tools\",\"standalone-baksmali\"]]\n# insert a note gap\ngaps.insert(1,{\"id\":\"generalize-before-stop\",\"concept\":\"carry the hand-solved method into solve.py when a live worker reaches CORRECT first\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"note\",\"detail\":\"D23: TT/Mastery were hand-solved (jadx + javac) while the generalize workers were cut off at CORRECT, so solve.py kept no v2 path and tomorrow's Mastery (which mixes old days, now regenerated as v2) would be silent again. Harness note: when a timed mode is CORRECT via a live worker, let one generalize worker finish (offline, no clock) and require a passing `hctf solver-test` on the variant-* cases with expected.json filled from confirmed.json (D23 variant cases have expected {}).\"})\nbuilt_prev=\"\"\"aab-proto-manifest-parse, ans-prefix-numeric-compose, anti-debug-state-machine-clean-path, apk-signing-block-payload,\nasset-cipher-dex-loader, asset-db-prefs-backup, attestation-jws-claims, binder-ontransact-code-map,\"\"\"\nassert built_prev in t\nt2=t[:a]\nsec=\"\"\"## Readiness gaps\n\nPriority 1 = plausible within ~3 days. \"prebuild\" = pure-python extractor in `lib/android.py` style that races in\n`solve.py`. \"tool\" = install. \"note\" = doc/prompt change. Already built (prebuild-state ok, dropped from the list):\naab-proto-manifest-parse, ans-prefix-numeric-compose, anti-debug-state-machine-clean-path, apk-signing-block-payload,\nasset-cipher-dex-loader, asset-db-prefs-backup, attestation-jws-claims, binder-ontransact-code-map,\nbiometric-auth-callback-eval, broadcast-receiver-action-map, cdex-vdex-string-pool, cert-and-signing-facts,\ncert-pin-and-nsc-facts, classloader-shadow-resolve, clean-device-env-stubs, custom-alphabet-decode,\ndalvik-mini-interpreter, dart-snapshot-string-pool, decode-any-chain-peel, decrypt-call-site-args-eval,\ndex-bytecode-integrity-gate, dex-gated-branch-consts, dex-native-call-args, dex-native-split-assembly,\ndex-slack-and-header-anomaly, dex-string-decrypt-arrays, dispatch-key-resolve, emulator-telephony-sensor-stubs,\nentry-reachable-callgraph-rank, enum-switchmap-state-resolve, exception-driven-control-flow, flattened-cfg-switch-eval,\nhermes-hbc-string-table, hook-framework-introspection-stubs, identifier-collision-resolve, identity-derived-key,\nil2cpp-metadata-literals, installer-source-and-tamper-probe-stubs, integrity-derived-key, java-serialized-object-parse,\njni-export-return-trace, jni-gate-bypass-input, jni-reflection-callback, jwt-token-decode-verify,\nkey-attestation-rootoftrust-parse, known-string-obfuscator-signatures, kotlin-metadata-names-and-coroutines,\nmessagedigest-derived-answer, module-contract-member-eval, multi-abi-arm-native, multi-stage-loader-recurse,\nnative-gated-branch-read, native-init-array-decrypt, native-inline-syscall-stubs, native-libc-probe-stubs-emulate,\nnative-payload-system-load, native-so-emulate-export, native-stack-string, native-system-property-and-mounts-stubs,\nnested-container-recurse, opaque-predicate-dead-branch, payload-digest-pinned-select,\npayload-magic-known-plaintext-unwrap, permutation-transposition-family, probe-arg-resolve-before-stub,\nprocess-exec-shell-probe-stubs, proguard-mapping-restore, proof-flow-candidate-ranking, protobuf-asset-wire-decode,\nproxy-methodhandle-invokecustom, puzzle-entry-pointer-follow, puzzle-indexed-and-perm-fields, r8-renamed-chain-follow,\nreflection-name-resolve, registernatives-table, resource-id-const-resolve, rolling-xor-keystream-family,\nroot-signal-vector-key, sqlcipher-asset-decrypt, static-key-cipher-decode, timing-and-debug-flag-probe-stubs,\ntiny-bytecode-vm-interpret, utf16-string-pool-scan, v1-manifest-digest-verify, webview-asset-js-scan,\nwhitebox-table-cipher-eval, xamarin-xalz-blob-unpack, zip-structure-anomaly-scan.\nForecast after D23: the MASVS-RESILIENCE arc continues one control per day (D21 anti-debug, D22 root, D23 hook/\ninstrumentation); still unnamed: emulator detection, tamper/repackaging/installer/signature, attestation (Play Integrity,\nkey attestation), then obfuscation capstones (flattening, VM, white-box). The big change is structural: since D23 the\ntimed builds (TT + every Mastery set, old days included) COMPUTE the answer in dex (`Release.code`), so each new theme\nwill most likely arrive as a gate fn / probe set inside that chain, and soon as real Android API reads through the\nContext it already receives. Priority 1 = a fast, sandbox-safe v2 evaluator (incl. JNI bridge and Context stubs).\n\n```json\n\"\"\"+json.dumps(gaps,indent=None,ensure_ascii=False).replace('}, {\"id\"','},\\n  {\"id\"').replace('[{\"id\"','[\\n  {\"id\"').replace('}]','}\\n]')+\"\"\"\n```\n\"\"\"\nopen(p,'w').write(t2+sec)\nPYEOF\npython3 $TMPDIR/gaps.py && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json,re\nt=open('reference/coverage/mobile-android.md').read()\ng=json.loads(re.search(r\"```json\\n(.*?)```\",t,re.S).group(1))\ns=json.load(open('.run/prebuild-state.json'))\npend=[x['id'] for x in g if x['action']=='prebuild' and not (s.get('mobile-android:'+x['id'],{}).get('ok') or s.get('mobile-android:'+x['id'],{}).get('attempts',0)>=2)]\nprint(len(g), 'pending prebuild', len(pend), pend)\nassert all(set(x)=={'id','concept','priority','action','detail'} for x in g)\nprint(len(set(x['id'] for x in g))==len(g))\nEOF\ntail -c 600 reference/coverage/mobile-android.md; wc -l reference/coverage/mobile-android.md"}}}
