{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgKFwF4e91L1VtjJLUgWD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both files are updated. Nothing else was touched, and no tests or GM calls were run.\n\nDay 23 changed how the lane works. The single solve was the usual v1 puzzle, `xor` with key 81, solved by the race probe in about 22 s. But the Time Trial and all 7 Mastery sets shipped a new puzzle format, `puzzle.v2` with `codec:\"analysis\"`. It has no data field: the answer is computed in the dex by `Release.code(Context)`, a chain of 64-bit mixing functions. That covered the old-day sets too: d02, d06, d10, d14, d15, d22 and d23. The d15 set also calls a native `nativeShare(long)` partway through the chain.\n\nThe carried-over solver found nothing on any v2 APK. Live workers solved them by hand: Time Trial in about 94 s and Mastery in about 2 min. The workers that should have generalised `solve.py` were stopped when the answers came back CORRECT, so `solve.py` still can't solve v2. Also, for set 5 a worker loaded the artifact's `.so` on the host with `ctypes.CDLL`, which breaks the sandbox rule. Both files now flag it as a pitfall.\n\n1. **`reference/techniques/mobile-android.md`** (now 171 lines; days 16–22 compressed):\n   - Added the Day 23 entry: the v1 single vs the v2 timed builds, the chain's structure, the decoy look-alike functions, the jadx + javac method that worked, timings, and the gap left in `solve.py`.\n   - Added variant axes for the puzzle schema (v1 vs v2) and for the shape of the computed chain, and updated the answer-location, Mastery-mix (7 sets) and native-lib axes.\n   - Added recognition cues for v2, the native call in the chain, and the `Probe` searches. New pitfalls: the single's shape differs from the timed shape, the solver wasn't generalised before the run stopped, regex-built `ANS-` decoys, and running artifact native code.\n\n2. **Coverage atlas, concept table and cues:** row 91 (hoo